1
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:05,780
(1 match, 1 win)

2
00:00:07,553 --> 00:00:11,520
(Current win rate: 100 percent)

3
00:00:12,913 --> 00:00:16,446
(The next opponent revealed)

4
00:00:24,346 --> 00:00:28,013
(Season 2's first match
in front of a live crowd)

5
00:00:32,813 --> 00:00:36,346
(Prove your potential...)

6
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:41,313
(in front of a packed house!)

7
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,113
(The opponent
for Season 2's first live match)

8
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:57,880
(Pink Spiders' Pyo Seung Ju)

9
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,280
Come on.

10
00:00:59,913 --> 00:01:01,580
I know her from somewhere.

11
00:01:05,966 --> 00:01:08,733
(Pink Spiders' Lee Na Yeon)

12
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:19,200
It's the Pink Spiders.

13
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:24,166
Hello, I'm the former captain
of the Wonder Dogs.

14
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,520
I used to play for the Wonder Dogs,

15
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:29,565
but now I'm with the Pink Spiders.

16
00:01:29,566 --> 00:01:33,932
I'm back with the Pink Spiders now.

17
00:01:33,933 --> 00:01:34,866
I'm Pyo Seung Ju.

18
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,233
I'm Lee Na Yeon.

19
00:01:38,347 --> 00:01:41,265
(Seung Ju and Na Yeon,
former starters for the Wonder Dogs)

20
00:01:41,266 --> 00:01:44,400
(Now back as starters
for the Pink Spiders)

21
00:01:47,766 --> 00:01:50,000
Seung Ju and Na Yeon are...

22
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,300
both players you can't take lightly.

23
00:01:54,866 --> 00:01:57,933
(One year ago)

24
00:01:58,566 --> 00:02:01,200
(Coach Yeon Koung's razor-sharp strategy)

25
00:02:02,333 --> 00:02:04,666
(Captain Seung Ju's targeted serve
hits home,)

26
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,433
(followed by Na Yeon's quick attack.)

27
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:10,300
(Outsmarting their rivals,)

28
00:02:11,466 --> 00:02:14,366
(they sweep the 2024-2025
pro league champions,)

29
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:17,366
(the Pink Spiders, 3 to 0.)

30
00:02:19,366 --> 00:02:22,733
I never thought we'd get swept 3 to 0.

31
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,766
It stung quite a bit.

32
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:35,265
After that match,
we went straight to the tape.

33
00:02:35,266 --> 00:02:38,066
We broke down what worked and what didn't.

34
00:02:39,233 --> 00:02:41,800
(During last year's match
against the Pink Spiders)

35
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:43,366
It's out!

36
00:02:46,933 --> 00:02:49,066
(Catching what everyone else missed)

37
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:53,133
(Nothing gets past his hawk eyes.)

38
00:02:54,833 --> 00:02:56,833
(Stringing together one successful
video challenge after another)

39
00:02:58,666 --> 00:03:00,465
(The coach with the eagle eye)

40
00:03:00,466 --> 00:03:05,366
We also broke down the Wonder Dogs'
strengths and weaknesses.

41
00:03:06,142 --> 00:03:11,199
Young In tends to favor sharp line shots.

42
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:14,465
Enkhsoyol rarely drives it
deep down the line.

43
00:03:14,466 --> 00:03:16,633
And Chae Rim...

44
00:03:18,966 --> 00:03:22,633
Chae Rim didn't get
many touches last year.

45
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,066
So we should be able
to keep her attack in check.

46
00:03:29,966 --> 00:03:33,100
(What do you think of the Wonder Dogs'
Season Two roster?)

47
00:03:37,166 --> 00:03:38,633
(Laughs)

48
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:42,933
I think Coach Yeon Koung has plenty
to lose sleep over.

49
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:50,700
I rate Seung Ju really highly,

50
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,700
so losing her weakens
their outside hitting.

51
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:00,733
Seung Ju's absence will definitely
hurt them the most.

52
00:04:01,233 --> 00:04:03,933
(All signs point...)

53
00:04:04,566 --> 00:04:06,900
(to the void left by Seung Ju.)

54
00:04:07,366 --> 00:04:09,432
(The Wonder Dogs...)

55
00:04:09,433 --> 00:04:11,700
(are down a key weapon.)

56
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:17,132
(What about their setting options
for Season Two?)

57
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:21,899
They've got a decent setter rotation,

58
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,133
so it isn't bad.

59
00:04:23,733 --> 00:04:26,900
Still, the overall level has dropped.

60
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:30,932
At the end of the day,
Na Yeon brought something...

61
00:04:30,933 --> 00:04:32,532
that Da Sol couldn't.

62
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:35,533
That's ultimately why Da Sol got cut.

63
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:41,332
They reached out to ask
if I'd join the Pink Spiders.

64
00:04:41,333 --> 00:04:43,733
I figured why not give it a shot,

65
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:46,032
so I went in for a tryout.

66
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:47,033
(Na Yeon returns to the pros
with the Pink Spiders)

67
00:04:48,266 --> 00:04:51,066
(Meanwhile, 13-year veteran
Da Sol is released.)

68
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:55,832
(Da Sol's evaluation at the mock draft)

69
00:04:55,833 --> 00:04:58,866
Da Sol has always been more of a backup...

70
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,065
than a starter.

71
00:05:01,066 --> 00:05:02,265
If Da Sol were good enough,

72
00:05:02,266 --> 00:05:04,733
they wouldn't have brought in Na Yeon.

73
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:07,433
I feel for Da Sol,

74
00:05:08,258 --> 00:05:12,624
but we need to show her
on the court today...

75
00:05:13,079 --> 00:05:16,279
the cold reality of pro sports.

76
00:05:20,529 --> 00:05:24,628
Plus, we've all seen Coach Yeon Koung...

77
00:05:24,629 --> 00:05:26,395
lose her temper before.

78
00:05:26,396 --> 00:05:32,829
I think that might get
in the players' heads too.

79
00:05:35,256 --> 00:05:36,923
Seung Ju and Na Yeon...

80
00:05:37,624 --> 00:05:40,057
As former Wonder Dogs,

81
00:05:40,151 --> 00:05:42,617
we can't go out there
and look sloppy against them.

82
00:05:43,092 --> 00:05:45,758
At the end of the day, we play to win,

83
00:05:45,759 --> 00:05:48,392
not just to hang in there.

84
00:05:49,059 --> 00:05:52,191
My Wonder Dogs days are behind me.

85
00:05:52,192 --> 00:05:54,959
I play for the Pink Spiders now,

86
00:05:55,392 --> 00:05:57,259
so I'm giving everything I've got
to take the win.

87
00:05:58,159 --> 00:06:01,624
Those two are the main reason...

88
00:06:01,625 --> 00:06:05,024
the Pink Spiders clicked so fast
as a team.

89
00:06:05,025 --> 00:06:07,959
I think we'll take it in a blowout.

90
00:06:08,325 --> 00:06:10,459
We've definitely got this.

91
00:06:13,625 --> 00:06:16,359
It's going to be a battle,

92
00:06:17,125 --> 00:06:19,292
but we can't let this one slip away.

93
00:06:19,559 --> 00:06:21,191
It won't be easy...

94
00:06:21,192 --> 00:06:23,049
since we know each other inside and out.

95
00:06:23,292 --> 00:06:27,024
Then again, we know
how Seung Ju plays too.

96
00:06:27,025 --> 00:06:28,658
We're not intimidated.

97
00:06:28,659 --> 00:06:30,559
We have Coach Yeon Koung in our corner.

98
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:34,159
This is going to be fun.

99
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:36,524
They were talking a big game.

100
00:06:36,525 --> 00:06:38,759
Sounded pretty confident, didn't they?

101
00:06:39,159 --> 00:06:41,058
Coach Dae Kyung also claimed...

102
00:06:41,059 --> 00:06:43,625
my temper would kill the team's morale.

103
00:06:44,692 --> 00:06:46,291
Shows what he knows.

104
00:06:46,292 --> 00:06:47,892
After the Shujitsu match,

105
00:06:48,159 --> 00:06:50,992
I know exactly
how to keep their energy up.

106
00:06:51,392 --> 00:06:53,959
(Fully evolved into a coach
who knows how to boost team morale)

107
00:06:55,259 --> 00:06:56,724
They're in for a rude awakening.

108
00:06:56,725 --> 00:07:00,459
Just wait until they see
how we played in match one.

109
00:07:01,079 --> 00:07:02,145
We'll dial in our game plan...

110
00:07:02,170 --> 00:07:04,203
and keep this win streak rolling.

111
00:07:06,109 --> 00:07:07,234
(Episode 4)

112
00:07:07,266 --> 00:07:07,995
(We Used to Be)

113
00:07:08,322 --> 00:07:11,771
(Video analysis
for the Pink Spiders match)

114
00:07:11,796 --> 00:07:13,363
Our targets are...

115
00:07:13,463 --> 00:07:15,630
Na Yeon and Seung Ju.

116
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:18,396
We're locking in on those two.

117
00:07:18,763 --> 00:07:20,373
You have to mark them tightly.

118
00:07:21,696 --> 00:07:25,263
Since Na Yeon will start,

119
00:07:25,496 --> 00:07:30,230
we'll target our serves deep to zone one.

120
00:07:30,363 --> 00:07:32,929
Either drive it deep
to zone one or drop it short.

121
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:34,229
(Target serve at zone 1)

122
00:07:34,230 --> 00:07:35,363
The reason is,

123
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:38,096
when the pass takes her to zone one,

124
00:07:39,063 --> 00:07:40,296
Na Yeon loses her touch,

125
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:42,730
and she rarely sets behind her.

126
00:07:43,563 --> 00:07:45,196
Off balls in zone one,

127
00:07:46,096 --> 00:07:48,930
she almost never goes to the right side.

128
00:07:50,096 --> 00:07:52,595
(Disrupt setter Na Yeon)

129
00:07:52,596 --> 00:07:54,096
So middle blockers,

130
00:07:54,596 --> 00:07:58,963
keep in mind they're going
to keep feeding the left pin.

131
00:07:59,263 --> 00:08:00,895
Read the play and commit.

132
00:08:00,896 --> 00:08:04,495
(Load up on the left-side attack.)

133
00:08:04,496 --> 00:08:07,863
We need that ball going into zone one...

134
00:08:08,430 --> 00:08:11,963
to control the tempo the way we want.

135
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:15,862
Second, whenever their setter
is in zone 4, 3, or 2,

136
00:08:15,863 --> 00:08:18,996
whenever Na Yeon rotates
into the front row,

137
00:08:19,796 --> 00:08:24,129
that's our window to pull away.

138
00:08:24,130 --> 00:08:26,129
Why do you think...

139
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:29,363
we can score in bunches
when she's in the front row?

140
00:08:30,130 --> 00:08:32,429
Because of her block height?

141
00:08:32,430 --> 00:08:33,279
Exactly.

142
00:08:33,343 --> 00:08:35,348
She doesn't have the height at the net.

143
00:08:35,693 --> 00:08:38,426
Because she's a low block,

144
00:08:38,693 --> 00:08:40,725
our hitters have an open lane to score.

145
00:08:40,726 --> 00:08:42,460
(Relentlessly attack over Na Yeon.)

146
00:08:43,493 --> 00:08:46,393
Keep going after Na Yeon's block...

147
00:08:46,593 --> 00:08:47,693
and run up the score.

148
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:50,393
Never take your mind off...

149
00:08:50,593 --> 00:08:53,460
hunting those matchups
and scoring points out there.

150
00:08:53,660 --> 00:08:54,725
- Understood?
- Yes.

151
00:08:54,726 --> 00:08:57,859
When Seung Ju gets a clean set,
she keeps finding the seam.

152
00:08:57,860 --> 00:09:01,726
So get your pin block set square,
especially in zone two.

153
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:04,925
If Seung Ju is up front, hit right at her.

154
00:09:04,926 --> 00:09:06,646
Seung Ju loves that push
to the deep middle.

155
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:10,892
Whenever she sees an opening,
she hits or tips straight into it.

156
00:09:10,893 --> 00:09:14,159
You have to know this inside and out.
It's the key to this match.

157
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:15,788
It's absolutely crucial.

158
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:20,860
Everyone steps onto the court
to win, obviously.

159
00:09:21,326 --> 00:09:22,395
Take it easy on them?

160
00:09:23,060 --> 00:09:24,964
Why would we ever go easy on them?

161
00:09:25,393 --> 00:09:27,493
Seung Ju and Na Yeon.

162
00:09:27,860 --> 00:09:31,460
We know their strengths
and weaknesses inside out,

163
00:09:31,593 --> 00:09:34,792
so we can exploit every
single one of them...

164
00:09:34,793 --> 00:09:36,075
and take care of business.

165
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:39,260
And today,

166
00:09:40,093 --> 00:09:41,560
we have a special guest.

167
00:09:43,193 --> 00:09:44,859
A new teammate has joined us.

168
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:45,860
(Approaching)

169
00:09:48,926 --> 00:09:50,460
(Realizing)

170
00:09:52,393 --> 00:09:53,393
All right.

171
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,292
- How've you been?
- Good!

172
00:09:55,293 --> 00:09:56,293
- Everything good?
- Yes.

173
00:09:56,326 --> 00:09:57,326
Tsubaki.

174
00:09:57,560 --> 00:09:58,925
Do you speak Korean?

175
00:09:58,926 --> 00:10:00,526
(Tanyama Tsubaki)

176
00:10:01,326 --> 00:10:03,893
I knew she'd make the team.

177
00:10:04,526 --> 00:10:07,726
I figured Tsubaki had to be
one of the final picks.

178
00:10:07,893 --> 00:10:11,126
Tsubaki was incredible at tryouts.

179
00:10:11,693 --> 00:10:15,560
Back during the Shujitsu match,
the locker room was already set up.

180
00:10:16,326 --> 00:10:19,593
(The locker room
during the Shujitsu match)

181
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:21,693
Two, four, six.

182
00:10:27,093 --> 00:10:28,560
Hey, Young In.

183
00:10:28,993 --> 00:10:30,193
There's an extra spot.

184
00:10:31,226 --> 00:10:33,125
There are 15. We have 15 lockers.

185
00:10:33,126 --> 00:10:34,992
(A 15th spot?)

186
00:10:34,993 --> 00:10:38,326
There was an open locker
over in the setter section.

187
00:10:39,193 --> 00:10:43,060
I wondered if another setter
was coming in,

188
00:10:43,126 --> 00:10:44,826
and sure enough, it was Tsubaki.

189
00:10:45,826 --> 00:10:47,625
Truth is, during tryouts,

190
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:51,093
we selected three setters.

191
00:10:51,426 --> 00:10:56,892
Tsubaki's arrival was delayed a bit
because of visa processing.

192
00:10:56,893 --> 00:10:58,524
Why don't you introduce yourself?

193
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,093
Hello.

194
00:11:00,593 --> 00:11:03,060
I'm Tsubaki from Japan.

195
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:05,693
- I'll give it my all. Thank you.
- Oh, wow.

196
00:11:05,718 --> 00:11:07,727
(Greeting in Korean?)

197
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:14,160
(Flashback to the tryout)

198
00:11:14,293 --> 00:11:16,826
(Scurrying over)

199
00:11:16,851 --> 00:11:19,338
(Tsubaki, setter)

200
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,693
Is she Japanese?

201
00:11:21,993 --> 00:11:24,292
- Have you seen "Haikyu!!"?
- Yeah, I have!

202
00:11:24,293 --> 00:11:25,825
She won the national championship
featured in that series.

203
00:11:25,826 --> 00:11:26,860
Really?

204
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:28,425
What birth year is she? Is she a baby?

205
00:11:28,426 --> 00:11:29,593
No clue.

206
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:36,193
I'm Tsubaki, setter
for the Kansai University volleyball team.

207
00:11:37,093 --> 00:11:38,460
I'm 19 years old.

208
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:39,926
Nice to meet you.

209
00:11:44,326 --> 00:11:45,960
(Passing)

210
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:47,492
(Crisp back set into a kill)

211
00:11:47,493 --> 00:11:48,793
- Nice!
- Beautiful set!

212
00:11:49,226 --> 00:11:50,293
Go!

213
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,393
(Setting)

214
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:54,026
(Lighting up the offense
with quick reflexes...)

215
00:11:55,126 --> 00:11:56,260
(Setting)

216
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:58,626
(and threading versatile pipe attacks)

217
00:11:59,026 --> 00:12:02,292
(Tsubaki commands the court
with total composure.)

218
00:12:02,293 --> 00:12:04,357
- It comes out so clean, doesn't it?
- Yeah, it's gorgeous.

219
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:06,926
It's set on a platter for the hitters.

220
00:12:09,526 --> 00:12:10,692
That Japanese girl can play.

221
00:12:10,693 --> 00:12:11,692
- Pretty solid, right?
- Yeah.

222
00:12:11,717 --> 00:12:14,617
Shibiki looks legit to me.

223
00:12:15,393 --> 00:12:16,426
She's got real touch.

224
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:19,372
I want to carry about three setters.

225
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,026
My picks are Da Sol,

226
00:12:21,526 --> 00:12:22,560
Hyo Rim,

227
00:12:22,793 --> 00:12:25,326
and Tsubaki. Those are my three.

228
00:12:26,093 --> 00:12:27,959
If Tsubaki can join right away,

229
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,282
she's my clear number two.

230
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:32,060
She's so well-rounded,
especially with her game management.

231
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:33,326
Agreed.

232
00:12:33,493 --> 00:12:35,093
- Same here.
- Totally agree.

233
00:12:36,193 --> 00:12:39,159
Japan plays great volleyball.

234
00:12:39,184 --> 00:12:42,650
What made you want to play here in Korea?

235
00:12:43,508 --> 00:12:48,234
My grandfather played for...

236
00:12:48,821 --> 00:12:51,654
the Korean national reserve team.

237
00:12:51,679 --> 00:12:54,611
(Her grandfather, Woo Gab Sik,
was a Korean national reserve player)

238
00:12:54,728 --> 00:13:00,628
So I've always wanted to test myself
in the Korean league.

239
00:13:01,095 --> 00:13:07,353
Since I have Korean heritage
and this door opened,

240
00:13:07,695 --> 00:13:10,527
I came here determined to prove myself.

241
00:13:10,861 --> 00:13:12,995
I hope you bring great energy
to the squad.

242
00:13:13,295 --> 00:13:14,760
Let's make it count together.

243
00:13:14,761 --> 00:13:17,395
(Welcome, Tsubaki.)

244
00:13:19,095 --> 00:13:20,928
Now that Tsubaki,

245
00:13:21,755 --> 00:13:24,255
our new youngest, has arrived,

246
00:13:24,761 --> 00:13:25,860
I was thrilled.

247
00:13:25,861 --> 00:13:26,960
(21 years old)

248
00:13:26,961 --> 00:13:29,608
She's so adorable
it just brought a huge smile to my face.

249
00:13:31,795 --> 00:13:33,479
I'm not the baby of the team anymore.

250
00:13:34,761 --> 00:13:36,760
Today, we're working on tempo serves...

251
00:13:36,761 --> 00:13:39,027
and hitting exact spots. Got it?

252
00:13:39,028 --> 00:13:40,061
- Yes, Coach.
- Yes, Coach.

253
00:13:40,195 --> 00:13:42,760
- Step up and serve right away.
- Serving!

254
00:13:42,761 --> 00:13:44,927
You earn two points
if you get it off fast...

255
00:13:44,928 --> 00:13:46,194
- and hit the target.
- Understood.

256
00:13:46,195 --> 00:13:47,126
All right.

257
00:13:47,528 --> 00:13:49,928
(Target speed: 65 km/h or higher)

258
00:13:50,461 --> 00:13:52,961
Hit that spot!

259
00:13:53,728 --> 00:13:54,967
Put it right in there.

260
00:13:55,188 --> 00:13:56,295
- Yes, Coach!
- Yes, Coach!

261
00:13:56,861 --> 00:13:59,195
(Relentlessly targeting zone one...)

262
00:13:59,828 --> 00:14:01,160
(to break Na Yeon's rhythm)

263
00:14:01,161 --> 00:14:02,827
- Just nail the target zone.
- Okay!

264
00:14:02,828 --> 00:14:03,909
Give me that clean ball.

265
00:14:04,928 --> 00:14:05,928
Serve.

266
00:14:08,595 --> 00:14:10,094
Nope. Sixty-two.

267
00:14:10,095 --> 00:14:11,095
(Both missed marks.)

268
00:14:11,961 --> 00:14:12,995
Sixty!

269
00:14:13,661 --> 00:14:14,661
Fifty-four.

270
00:14:15,481 --> 00:14:16,243
Long!

271
00:14:16,267 --> 00:14:18,761
Step into it! You have to hit the mark!

272
00:14:19,461 --> 00:14:21,395
Faster!

273
00:14:21,495 --> 00:14:23,295
Paint the line!

274
00:14:26,361 --> 00:14:27,428
Sixty-six!

275
00:14:27,661 --> 00:14:29,027
There you go!

276
00:14:29,028 --> 00:14:30,328
(That's how it's done!)

277
00:14:31,828 --> 00:14:32,827
Sixty-seven.

278
00:14:32,828 --> 00:14:34,661
That's the one! Great ball!

279
00:14:35,295 --> 00:14:37,395
(Finding the groove after reps)

280
00:14:37,661 --> 00:14:39,661
Yes! Great serve!

281
00:14:39,861 --> 00:14:42,260
That's it! Right on the money!

282
00:14:42,261 --> 00:14:43,260
(Beaming with pride)

283
00:14:43,261 --> 00:14:44,861
(Enkhsoyol steps up.)

284
00:14:46,895 --> 00:14:48,095
Wait, what?

285
00:14:49,195 --> 00:14:51,328
(Embarrassed)

286
00:14:52,261 --> 00:14:53,928
(Dialing back in)

287
00:14:56,128 --> 00:14:59,328
Not zone six!

288
00:15:00,028 --> 00:15:01,028
(Resetting for another try)

289
00:15:02,128 --> 00:15:03,728
I said, "Stay out of zone six!"

290
00:15:04,628 --> 00:15:06,195
(Pouting)

291
00:15:09,828 --> 00:15:11,677
- No, that wasn't even close!
- What was that?

292
00:15:12,061 --> 00:15:14,213
- No, that wasn't even close!
- What was that?

293
00:15:15,895 --> 00:15:16,961
Huh?

294
00:15:18,228 --> 00:15:20,161
(Groaning in frustration)

295
00:15:22,528 --> 00:15:23,527
Enkhsoyol.

296
00:15:23,528 --> 00:15:25,461
You're not supposed to snipe
the other team's coach.

297
00:15:26,061 --> 00:15:27,061
Yes, Coach.

298
00:15:28,728 --> 00:15:30,828
Keep it in the court.

299
00:15:32,614 --> 00:15:34,633
She gives away so many points
on serve errors.

300
00:15:34,995 --> 00:15:36,961
Enkhsoyol clearly has the talent,

301
00:15:37,261 --> 00:15:39,104
which makes it even more frustrating.

302
00:15:39,695 --> 00:15:41,760
She has all the tools,
especially that natural frame.

303
00:15:41,761 --> 00:15:43,860
Both her parents were athletes,

304
00:15:43,861 --> 00:15:46,028
so the athletic pedigree is there.

305
00:15:46,461 --> 00:15:47,895
I just wish she'd put it all together...

306
00:15:48,061 --> 00:15:50,295
and take her game to the next level.

307
00:15:50,795 --> 00:15:54,028
Instead, she makes choices on the court
that leave you scratching your head.

308
00:15:54,295 --> 00:15:57,356
It's tough to watch when she has
that much raw physical ability.

309
00:15:58,561 --> 00:15:59,560
Serve!

310
00:15:59,561 --> 00:16:00,595
(Serve drills press on.)

311
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:03,295
Out.

312
00:16:04,228 --> 00:16:05,228
(Sighs heavily)

313
00:16:06,395 --> 00:16:07,861
(Looking on)

314
00:16:10,295 --> 00:16:13,627
(Punishing conditioning
right on the heels of the Shujitsu match)

315
00:16:13,628 --> 00:16:14,695
Serve.

316
00:16:15,661 --> 00:16:16,661
(Groaning)

317
00:16:17,361 --> 00:16:19,528
(The squad is visibly gassed
from the brutal session.)

318
00:16:22,261 --> 00:16:23,494
- Are you finished?
- Not yet.

319
00:16:23,495 --> 00:16:25,161
- Getting lightheaded?
- My head's spinning.

320
00:16:26,228 --> 00:16:28,028
- Dizzy? Go grab some water.
- Okay.

321
00:16:29,095 --> 00:16:30,127
(Sighing)

322
00:16:30,128 --> 00:16:32,828
Min Kyeong, why are you so pale?

323
00:16:33,121 --> 00:16:34,154
Are you feeling dizzy?

324
00:16:34,895 --> 00:16:35,895
You as well?

325
00:16:36,361 --> 00:16:37,361
Lightheaded?

326
00:16:37,595 --> 00:16:39,494
I haven't felt right since yesterday.

327
00:16:39,495 --> 00:16:42,728
(Even Min Kyeong is running on empty.)

328
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:45,295
Oh, boy.

329
00:16:47,995 --> 00:16:50,442
(Enkhsoyol hits the wall in training too.)

330
00:16:52,129 --> 00:16:54,562
(Frustrated)

331
00:16:55,735 --> 00:16:56,734
Does it hurt a lot?

332
00:16:56,735 --> 00:16:58,234
It feels a bit swollen.

333
00:16:58,235 --> 00:16:59,235
Swollen?

334
00:16:59,502 --> 00:17:00,767
Like it's puffing up.

335
00:17:00,768 --> 00:17:01,635
It's throbbing.

336
00:17:03,774 --> 00:17:04,808
Loosen your laces.

337
00:17:06,302 --> 00:17:10,368
(Her foot injury flares up again.)

338
00:17:13,635 --> 00:17:15,635
The girls are running on fumes.
This isn't good.

339
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:18,502
(Groans)

340
00:17:20,002 --> 00:17:23,934
Min Kyeong looked pale as a ghost earlier
and said she felt sick.

341
00:17:23,935 --> 00:17:25,136
Once she got some water
and caught her breath,

342
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:25,935
she said she was fine.

343
00:17:26,935 --> 00:17:28,047
What's Enkhsoyol doing over there?

344
00:17:28,268 --> 00:17:30,902
She says her foot is bothering her.

345
00:17:31,168 --> 00:17:32,701
Why is she just sitting there
without saying a word to me?

346
00:17:32,702 --> 00:17:34,020
- What?
- Without giving me a heads-up.

347
00:17:34,068 --> 00:17:35,654
Why is she just parked on the bench?

348
00:17:36,650 --> 00:17:41,661
Apparently, she landed awkwardly
on one foot, and it flared up.

349
00:17:46,850 --> 00:17:48,715
Everyone looks completely wiped out.

350
00:17:48,716 --> 00:17:50,050
I'm running on empty too.

351
00:17:50,816 --> 00:17:52,616
Are you okay?

352
00:17:53,683 --> 00:17:55,150
No, my body just won't listen.

353
00:17:55,502 --> 00:17:58,102
I couldn't even make clean contact
on the ball today.

354
00:18:01,650 --> 00:18:03,816
- You're rushing your approach.
- Damn it.

355
00:18:06,550 --> 00:18:09,682
(Serves keep spraying wide.)

356
00:18:09,707 --> 00:18:11,212
They're just mindlessly swatting at it.

357
00:18:14,716 --> 00:18:17,650
(Even Yeon Joo sends hers long.)

358
00:18:19,916 --> 00:18:23,350
(Practice continues
with three players sidelined.)

359
00:18:23,750 --> 00:18:25,538
They look totally flat out there.

360
00:18:26,116 --> 00:18:27,440
Every single one of them.

361
00:18:29,116 --> 00:18:32,616
(With the Pink Spiders match
right around the corner,)

362
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:35,282
(Coach Kim's anxiety mounts.)

363
00:18:35,283 --> 00:18:37,450
(Sighs)

364
00:18:37,583 --> 00:18:41,816
When players go down
with injuries or illness,

365
00:18:42,816 --> 00:18:44,449
it drags the whole team down.

366
00:18:44,450 --> 00:18:47,082
Everyone looks drained.

367
00:18:47,083 --> 00:18:49,083
That sluggish energy is contagious.

368
00:18:52,016 --> 00:18:54,650
That's what really frustrates me.

369
00:18:55,183 --> 00:18:59,515
We need high-intensity reps
to be game-ready.

370
00:18:59,516 --> 00:19:02,283
If they can't even handle
basic practice volume,

371
00:19:02,983 --> 00:19:05,682
how am I supposed to run this team?

372
00:19:05,683 --> 00:19:07,250
It's seriously worrying.

373
00:19:09,650 --> 00:19:10,883
Bring it in, everyone.

374
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:22,950
You don't get to play matches
if you can't put in the work at practice.

375
00:19:22,975 --> 00:19:23,514
Yes.

376
00:19:23,683 --> 00:19:25,182
Let me remind you again.

377
00:19:25,183 --> 00:19:26,733
We have exactly two months.

378
00:19:27,216 --> 00:19:28,849
That's seven matches.

379
00:19:28,850 --> 00:19:30,583
Four losses, and this program is over.

380
00:19:30,916 --> 00:19:35,082
Our objective is to build
a legitimate pro team.

381
00:19:35,083 --> 00:19:38,850
You need to understand that every loss
puts that dream on the line.

382
00:19:40,616 --> 00:19:44,982
I know injuries happen,

383
00:19:44,983 --> 00:19:47,949
but managing your physical readiness
is your responsibility.

384
00:19:47,950 --> 00:19:51,883
Taking care of your body is
rule number one for a pro athlete,

385
00:19:51,907 --> 00:19:52,591
isn't it?

386
00:19:56,583 --> 00:19:59,666
I'm looking directly at the three of you.

387
00:19:59,876 --> 00:20:01,827
The three of you. I'm serious.

388
00:20:05,350 --> 00:20:08,183
Watching players sit out
on the sidelines like this...

389
00:20:08,583 --> 00:20:10,749
makes my blood boil.

390
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,078
I don't care how talented you are.

391
00:20:16,483 --> 00:20:20,450
If this team is going
to make a habit of skipping reps,

392
00:20:21,650 --> 00:20:23,950
we might as well pack it up
and not practice at all.

393
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:31,319
If this were my call alone,
I'd cut all three of you...

394
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:34,000
from this roster right now.

395
00:20:36,853 --> 00:20:39,839
This is the reason I pushed for the power
to make roster cuts anytime.

396
00:20:40,487 --> 00:20:41,319
You're dragging your feet,

397
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:44,287
phoning it in, and showing
zero competitive fire.

398
00:20:48,287 --> 00:20:50,558
Lacking skill is one thing,

399
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:52,553
lacking heart is entirely unacceptable.

400
00:20:57,753 --> 00:20:58,858
We're done for today.

401
00:21:01,287 --> 00:21:03,387
- Pilseung!
- Wonder Dogs!

402
00:21:07,153 --> 00:21:09,652
As a coach, my emotions were torn.

403
00:21:09,653 --> 00:21:12,852
I felt the group desperately
needed a wake-up call,

404
00:21:12,853 --> 00:21:15,786
so I had to be tough on them.

405
00:21:15,787 --> 00:21:17,820
(Tough love for the sake of the team)

406
00:21:25,653 --> 00:21:27,420
I knew she was completely right.

407
00:21:27,853 --> 00:21:30,120
Conditioning and recovery are part
of being a professional.

408
00:21:30,487 --> 00:21:32,820
You can't get meaningful reps
when your body is broken.

409
00:21:33,387 --> 00:21:36,087
Every word she said was true.

410
00:21:36,853 --> 00:21:41,852
Since it's a bone issue,
medical treatment can only do so much.

411
00:21:41,853 --> 00:21:43,619
I have so much ground to make up
and so much to prove,

412
00:21:43,620 --> 00:21:44,952
so sitting out with this foot injury...

413
00:21:44,953 --> 00:21:49,986
leaves me wondering
how I'm even helping the team.

414
00:21:49,987 --> 00:21:52,453
My mind has just been racing.

415
00:21:54,053 --> 00:21:55,444
Back during my time in the pros,

416
00:21:55,468 --> 00:21:57,316
I pushed through
so much extra training alone.

417
00:21:57,453 --> 00:21:59,487
I assumed my body could take the pounding,

418
00:22:00,153 --> 00:22:01,820
but it eventually broke down.

419
00:22:02,753 --> 00:22:04,786
This was how it started.

420
00:22:04,787 --> 00:22:08,719
I didn't even realize I was injured
when I was with the Red Sparks.

421
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:11,386
Every time I planted to spike,
it was sharp pain.

422
00:22:11,387 --> 00:22:14,152
A lot of that is on me, though.

423
00:22:14,153 --> 00:22:16,286
I should've spoken up sooner.

424
00:22:16,287 --> 00:22:19,119
I think I put too much pressure on myself.

425
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:22,520
I tried to make massive leaps overnight...

426
00:22:23,087 --> 00:22:25,352
and ended up running my body
into the ground.

427
00:22:25,353 --> 00:22:27,452
That's when the foot gave out.

428
00:22:27,453 --> 00:22:31,952
Because of the injury,
my court time evaporated.

429
00:22:31,988 --> 00:22:33,854
It cut deep.

430
00:22:35,147 --> 00:22:36,747
(Even back at the mock draft)

431
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:40,547
Her toe injury turned out
to be a stress fracture.

432
00:22:41,114 --> 00:22:43,562
That doesn't just heal
on its own overnight.

433
00:22:44,353 --> 00:22:48,285
(Her injury was an immediate red flag
for front-office scouts.)

434
00:22:48,310 --> 00:22:49,915
Kids eat so much better these days.

435
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:51,789
- Processed foods!
- Exactly.

436
00:22:52,643 --> 00:22:54,442
(Tsk-tsk)

437
00:22:54,443 --> 00:22:56,509
They grow up on processed snacks...

438
00:22:56,510 --> 00:22:58,310
which ruins their bone density.

439
00:22:59,843 --> 00:23:05,209
(Her injury triggers a debate
on fast-food diets.)

440
00:23:05,210 --> 00:23:06,976
The thing is...

441
00:23:06,977 --> 00:23:08,909
I never really eat that stuff.

442
00:23:08,910 --> 00:23:10,976
I don't touch burgers or ramyeon.

443
00:23:10,977 --> 00:23:12,376
I barely even drink soda.

444
00:23:12,377 --> 00:23:13,909
I cut all of that out years ago.

445
00:23:13,910 --> 00:23:16,642
Growing up in Mongolia,

446
00:23:16,643 --> 00:23:19,676
my diet was packed with fresh dairy
and plenty of clean meat.

447
00:23:19,677 --> 00:23:21,534
I've always had an ironclad constitution.

448
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:28,643
(A Mongolian powerhouse
raised on pure, whole foods)

449
00:23:29,410 --> 00:23:33,709
I grew up strong as an ox,

450
00:23:33,710 --> 00:23:36,877
so I couldn't comprehend
how I ended up with a stress fracture.

451
00:23:39,210 --> 00:23:44,136
Why did this have to happen right now?

452
00:23:44,161 --> 00:23:45,477
It broke my heart.

453
00:23:46,377 --> 00:23:51,543
Being sidelined from volleyball
made it such a dark period.

454
00:23:52,443 --> 00:23:54,410
I missed my family terribly.

455
00:23:54,877 --> 00:23:58,276
When I first moved to Korea,
my little brother was...

456
00:23:58,277 --> 00:23:59,609
just a little toddler.

457
00:23:59,610 --> 00:24:02,009
Before I knew it,
he was practically all grown up.

458
00:24:02,010 --> 00:24:03,843
It left me with such an empty,
complicated feeling.

459
00:24:03,911 --> 00:24:09,178
Seeing my parents getting older
right before my eyes broke my heart too.

460
00:24:09,614 --> 00:24:11,950
I was burned out.

461
00:24:13,347 --> 00:24:16,181
If it hadn't been for the Wonder Dogs,

462
00:24:17,647 --> 00:24:20,380
I probably would've packed my bags
and gone home to Mongolia.

463
00:24:20,381 --> 00:24:21,681
(Waging a war on two fronts:
physical and mental)

464
00:24:22,140 --> 00:24:23,607
- Speak up when it flares up again.
- Okay.

465
00:24:24,681 --> 00:24:25,446
What's the issue?

466
00:24:25,447 --> 00:24:28,013
She says the padding under her foot
feels like it's shifting.

467
00:24:28,014 --> 00:24:28,814
Is she in pain?

468
00:24:29,114 --> 00:24:31,046
(Coach Kim has kept a watchful eye
on Enkhsoyol all along.)

469
00:24:31,047 --> 00:24:32,314
Thank goodness.

470
00:24:33,614 --> 00:24:36,881
(Even on the day
she read the team the riot act,)

471
00:24:37,314 --> 00:24:42,714
(she never once stopped worrying
about Enkhsoyol's foot.)

472
00:24:45,874 --> 00:24:47,356
What are we going to do with Enkhsoyol?

473
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:48,580
That foot is still giving her trouble.

474
00:24:48,847 --> 00:24:49,680
Enkhsoyol.

475
00:24:49,681 --> 00:24:54,681
(Another session kicks off
under the shadow of Enkhsoyol's injury.)

476
00:24:55,047 --> 00:24:57,981
The doctors told her to stop
all running and jumping.

477
00:24:59,281 --> 00:25:01,266
With our thin rotation,
that's almost impossible.

478
00:25:01,947 --> 00:25:03,480
I'm constantly worried about Enkhsoyol.

479
00:25:03,481 --> 00:25:07,113
We need Enkhsoyol firing
as our primary offensive weapon.

480
00:25:07,114 --> 00:25:08,807
Unless she rediscovers her rhythm,

481
00:25:09,181 --> 00:25:14,046
I don't see how this team
gets back on track.

482
00:25:14,047 --> 00:25:15,580
With our backs against the wall,

483
00:25:16,514 --> 00:25:20,581
what is it going to take
to turn this ship around?

484
00:25:21,347 --> 00:25:22,647
How do we fix this?

485
00:25:23,190 --> 00:25:25,356
That question runs through my head
all day long.

486
00:25:25,381 --> 00:25:28,447
(Carrying the weight of the team
on her own shoulders)

487
00:25:28,847 --> 00:25:33,398
I could tell she was carrying
a heavy burden herself.

488
00:25:33,450 --> 00:25:36,084
If she wants to break through her limits,

489
00:25:36,085 --> 00:25:38,453
she has to change somehow.

490
00:25:38,869 --> 00:25:42,972
I want to give her every chance...

491
00:25:43,260 --> 00:25:44,293
to get back on her feet.

492
00:25:46,297 --> 00:25:47,364
I'm done.

493
00:25:47,365 --> 00:25:48,898
(Against the Pink Spiders, D-3)

494
00:25:48,899 --> 00:25:50,567
Outside hitters only, over here.

495
00:25:51,402 --> 00:25:53,036
- Want me to serve?
- Yeah, hit it.

496
00:25:53,439 --> 00:25:54,620
Give me ten sets.

497
00:25:54,645 --> 00:25:56,072
(Special cross-court clinic begins.)

498
00:25:56,073 --> 00:25:58,006
Try cutting the angle like this.

499
00:25:58,007 --> 00:25:59,575
You don't need to muscle it.

500
00:25:59,576 --> 00:26:01,144
- The arm swing is what matters.
- Yes, Coach.

501
00:26:02,513 --> 00:26:03,713
(Ball sails out of bounds.)

502
00:26:04,014 --> 00:26:05,681
Watch the back of your hand.

503
00:26:06,551 --> 00:26:08,552
(Mimicking Enkhsoyol's straight swing)

504
00:26:08,553 --> 00:26:10,487
Snap your wrist outward on contact.

505
00:26:10,488 --> 00:26:11,321
Picture the direction.

506
00:26:11,665 --> 00:26:12,653
Pull back first...

507
00:26:12,678 --> 00:26:15,058
See how my wrist turns?

508
00:26:15,059 --> 00:26:16,308
This is where your palm should finish.

509
00:26:18,362 --> 00:26:19,195
Right there.

510
00:26:19,864 --> 00:26:21,197
From here...

511
00:26:21,198 --> 00:26:22,767
(1-on-1 coaching)

512
00:26:22,768 --> 00:26:24,267
- to here.
- Outward.

513
00:26:27,453 --> 00:26:28,071
Okay.

514
00:26:28,205 --> 00:26:31,506
Keeping it inside the lines matters,

515
00:26:31,507 --> 00:26:33,409
but mechanics matter just as much now.

516
00:26:33,410 --> 00:26:35,578
Snap your wrist across,

517
00:26:35,579 --> 00:26:38,815
or push up through the ball...

518
00:26:38,816 --> 00:26:40,650
Mixing up your shots
opens up sharper angles.

519
00:26:40,651 --> 00:26:42,785
The whole court will open up to you.

520
00:26:42,786 --> 00:26:45,087
When you go up to swing,

521
00:26:45,088 --> 00:26:47,223
you'll be able to paint anywhere
from three o'clock...

522
00:26:47,468 --> 00:26:49,302
to ten o'clock.

523
00:26:49,327 --> 00:26:51,060
Look at how much court you can cover.

524
00:26:51,061 --> 00:26:51,928
Do you see it?

525
00:26:52,263 --> 00:26:54,230
Imagine having that kind of range.

526
00:26:54,231 --> 00:26:55,965
Picture how great that would feel.

527
00:26:55,966 --> 00:26:57,867
- It would be unreal.
- Yes.

528
00:26:57,868 --> 00:26:59,845
We're drilling this
so you can hit every single angle.

529
00:26:59,870 --> 00:27:00,786
Got it?

530
00:27:01,072 --> 00:27:02,905
Snap the wrist. Snap it.

531
00:27:03,641 --> 00:27:04,441
All right.

532
00:27:04,675 --> 00:27:05,541
Your hand slipped back to this.

533
00:27:05,542 --> 00:27:07,043
(Reverting right back
to the straight shot)

534
00:27:07,411 --> 00:27:09,295
I think I'm starting
to get the feel for it.

535
00:27:09,781 --> 00:27:11,563
I need to finish with my palm turned out.

536
00:27:13,050 --> 00:27:14,150
That's right.

537
00:27:15,152 --> 00:27:16,052
(Landing in the court)

538
00:27:16,585 --> 00:27:17,386
It's clicking.

539
00:27:18,455 --> 00:27:19,688
More delicately this time.

540
00:27:19,713 --> 00:27:21,007
(Flawless angle and form)

541
00:27:21,032 --> 00:27:22,360
That's right!

542
00:27:22,893 --> 00:27:24,595
Keep your shoulder alignment in mind.

543
00:27:24,596 --> 00:27:27,030
Now try lifting your arms.

544
00:27:27,031 --> 00:27:28,364
Feel how tight that gets?

545
00:27:28,653 --> 00:27:29,632
- Get it now?
- Yes.

546
00:27:30,300 --> 00:27:31,166
Mine!

547
00:27:31,191 --> 00:27:33,992
(Making a breakthrough)

548
00:27:35,640 --> 00:27:39,742
Private reps make a huge difference.

549
00:27:39,743 --> 00:27:41,644
When Coach explains it,

550
00:27:41,645 --> 00:27:45,230
it clicks right away.

551
00:27:45,716 --> 00:27:48,117
Every word she says just sinks in.

552
00:27:48,118 --> 00:27:50,636
Enkhsoyol has come a long way
since last season.

553
00:27:50,954 --> 00:27:52,889
This is only the beginning, though.

554
00:27:52,890 --> 00:27:54,590
This is the part that counts.

555
00:27:55,026 --> 00:27:59,262
I want to see her keep leveling up.

556
00:28:03,693 --> 00:28:06,134
The second ball.

557
00:28:06,462 --> 00:28:07,830
What a shame.

558
00:28:08,385 --> 00:28:10,222
How do you say "You're bad at this"
in Mongolian?

559
00:28:10,607 --> 00:28:11,807
"You're bad at this?"

560
00:28:12,617 --> 00:28:14,977
- Chi chadakhgüi.
- Chichadko?

561
00:28:16,280 --> 00:28:18,047
(Awkward chuckle)

562
00:28:18,449 --> 00:28:19,098
Ball!

563
00:28:20,098 --> 00:28:22,116
(Diving dig falls short)

564
00:28:22,519 --> 00:28:23,652
Chadko!

565
00:28:24,644 --> 00:28:26,722
(The moment another error happens...)

566
00:28:26,723 --> 00:28:27,890
Chadko!

567
00:28:27,891 --> 00:28:28,958
Nope.

568
00:28:29,226 --> 00:28:30,826
- Second ball!
- Out right!

569
00:28:30,827 --> 00:28:31,661
(Crisp second-ball contact this time)

570
00:28:31,662 --> 00:28:33,162
That's the one!

571
00:28:33,163 --> 00:28:35,331
(Great pass, Enkhsoyol.)

572
00:28:35,332 --> 00:28:36,732
Beautifully done.

573
00:28:37,801 --> 00:28:40,369
How do you say "Nice" in Mongolian?

574
00:28:40,838 --> 00:28:43,040
- Sain.
- Sain?

575
00:28:43,041 --> 00:28:43,856
Yes.

576
00:28:46,143 --> 00:28:47,277
(Great dig)

577
00:28:47,278 --> 00:28:48,411
That's it! Sain!

578
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:49,963
Mine.

579
00:28:50,848 --> 00:28:52,364
Nice!

580
00:28:52,449 --> 00:28:53,316
Sain.

581
00:28:54,351 --> 00:28:55,285
(Dug)

582
00:28:55,286 --> 00:28:57,053
There you go. Nice.

583
00:28:57,054 --> 00:28:57,987
(Showering compliments)

584
00:28:57,988 --> 00:28:58,988
Sain.

585
00:28:58,989 --> 00:29:01,090
(Against the Pink Spiders, D-2)

586
00:29:01,091 --> 00:29:03,526
(Trainer Lee Sang Wha)

587
00:29:03,527 --> 00:29:04,794
(Doctor says Enkhsoyol's
stress fracture...)

588
00:29:04,795 --> 00:29:07,797
(has shown massive improvement.)

589
00:29:07,798 --> 00:29:08,731
Quick.

590
00:29:09,299 --> 00:29:10,799
That's it!

591
00:29:11,168 --> 00:29:12,584
Great swing, Enkhsoyol.

592
00:29:13,270 --> 00:29:14,103
Push it deep!

593
00:29:15,472 --> 00:29:17,072
Right there!

594
00:29:17,441 --> 00:29:19,575
Why did you think
that's the better choice?

595
00:29:19,843 --> 00:29:21,810
I lose a point
if it gets caught in the net.

596
00:29:21,811 --> 00:29:23,546
- It's better to go over the net.
- Bingo.

597
00:29:23,547 --> 00:29:24,780
(Not bad at all.)

598
00:29:25,308 --> 00:29:27,609
Are you a volleyball savant, Enkhsoyol?

599
00:29:27,885 --> 00:29:28,852
(Blushing)

600
00:29:28,999 --> 00:29:30,553
Back in Season One,

601
00:29:30,721 --> 00:29:33,222
things just flew right over her head.

602
00:29:33,557 --> 00:29:37,593
She looks like a totally
different player now.

603
00:29:37,594 --> 00:29:39,294
I feel completely different
compared to last year.

604
00:29:39,295 --> 00:29:40,663
This season, when I...

605
00:29:40,964 --> 00:29:41,798
(Chuckles)

606
00:29:41,799 --> 00:29:43,666
When I say "yes,"

607
00:29:43,667 --> 00:29:45,968
I genuinely mean it from the heart.

608
00:29:46,203 --> 00:29:48,237
I actually have fun learning while I play.

609
00:29:50,467 --> 00:29:51,434
Seventy-seven.

610
00:29:51,787 --> 00:29:53,024
There it is.

611
00:29:54,678 --> 00:29:55,778
(Serve upgrade unlocked)

612
00:29:55,779 --> 00:29:56,879
Nice!

613
00:29:57,614 --> 00:29:58,331
(Take this.)

614
00:29:59,249 --> 00:30:00,683
Dang it.

615
00:30:01,451 --> 00:30:02,351
Keep going.

616
00:30:03,020 --> 00:30:05,103
Why are you swinging at balls sailing out?

617
00:30:06,056 --> 00:30:07,023
That one stung.

618
00:30:08,352 --> 00:30:11,253
Pretty sure she was aiming for me.
She's so dead after this.

619
00:30:12,329 --> 00:30:14,363
I can feel the seam imprinted on my back.

620
00:30:14,765 --> 00:30:15,948
That was 100 percent personal.

621
00:30:16,235 --> 00:30:17,567
No way she swung that deep by accident.

622
00:30:17,568 --> 00:30:20,669
I know we've got what it takes.

623
00:30:20,670 --> 00:30:22,154
We have to figure it out.

624
00:30:24,207 --> 00:30:25,174
(Against the Pink Spiders, D-1)

625
00:30:25,175 --> 00:30:27,309
- That's right.
- Nice.

626
00:30:28,512 --> 00:30:30,513
(Enkhsoyol's rise fires up
the entire squad.)

627
00:30:30,514 --> 00:30:32,081
Good ball!

628
00:30:32,082 --> 00:30:33,716
That's it! Beautifully executed!

629
00:30:34,518 --> 00:30:35,518
(Clap)

630
00:30:35,519 --> 00:30:38,303
I feel so much more confident
we can pull this off.

631
00:30:38,455 --> 00:30:40,005
I'm going to give everything I have...

632
00:30:40,224 --> 00:30:41,691
to take down the Pink Spiders.

633
00:30:43,560 --> 00:30:47,229
(Ansan, Gyeonggi Province)

634
00:30:47,444 --> 00:30:50,623
Sangnoksu Arena was chosen as the venue.

635
00:30:52,442 --> 00:30:55,511
(Season 2's first live crowd)

636
00:30:59,711 --> 00:31:02,079
(Once ticket registration opened,)

637
00:31:03,181 --> 00:31:06,283
(an eye-popping 25,000 fans
applied in three days.)

638
00:31:06,618 --> 00:31:09,401
(A ruthless 12.5-to-1 ticketing lottery)

639
00:31:09,587 --> 00:31:12,997
To prove the team's star power,

640
00:31:13,485 --> 00:31:15,173
why not make a statement...

641
00:31:15,273 --> 00:31:17,268
with ticket sales and fan turnout?

642
00:31:17,329 --> 00:31:18,184
(Fan draw)

643
00:31:18,209 --> 00:31:19,042
(Pro franchise expansion checklist)

644
00:31:19,067 --> 00:31:21,059
(Front office, home market,
corporate sponsors, fan draw, performance)

645
00:31:27,853 --> 00:31:30,221
(Rallying behind the Wonder Dogs)

646
00:31:30,222 --> 00:31:31,856
(The Flame Deer Is Back,
Our Baby Enkhsoyol)

647
00:31:31,857 --> 00:31:36,427
(A full house unites today.)

648
00:31:36,762 --> 00:31:38,597
("Yes-soyol" said it again today!)

649
00:31:38,598 --> 00:31:40,999
(A Wonder Dogs win is
the ultimate birthday gift for me.)

650
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:43,134
(Coach Yeon Koung's parents)

651
00:31:43,535 --> 00:31:45,236
(Bo Bin's mother)

652
00:31:45,838 --> 00:31:47,439
(Ye Eun's father)

653
00:31:47,906 --> 00:31:49,406
(Young In's mother)

654
00:31:50,042 --> 00:31:51,976
(Suwon City head coach Kang Min Sik)

655
00:31:52,544 --> 00:31:54,745
(Former AI Peppers coach Chang So Yun,
former national team star Kang Hye Mi)

656
00:31:55,180 --> 00:31:56,914
(KOVO executive director Lee Young Ho)

657
00:31:57,516 --> 00:31:59,117
(Actresses Bang Hyo Rin,
Ko Sung Hee, and Lee Ha Nee)

658
00:31:59,785 --> 00:32:02,287
(Even national news cameras are rolling.)

659
00:32:02,454 --> 00:32:06,157
Our immediate goal is stacking wins.

660
00:32:06,158 --> 00:32:08,460
The dream we're all chasing...

661
00:32:08,693 --> 00:32:11,929
is founding that eighth franchise.

662
00:32:12,998 --> 00:32:14,732
(Meanwhile)

663
00:32:14,967 --> 00:32:17,734
Hello, and a huge welcome
to everyone packing the house...

664
00:32:17,758 --> 00:32:19,538
for the Pink Spiders
versus the Wonder Dogs!

665
00:32:19,872 --> 00:32:21,806
I'm your general manager and...

666
00:32:22,074 --> 00:32:23,875
head of PR for the Wonder Dogs,

667
00:32:24,243 --> 00:32:26,310
Boo Seung Kwan. Great to see you all!

668
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:30,882
(Manager Boo bags a promo.)

669
00:32:32,284 --> 00:32:33,201
(Getting arrogant)

670
00:32:33,226 --> 00:32:33,994
Oh, really?

671
00:32:34,019 --> 00:32:36,920
So I handle PR, branding,

672
00:32:36,921 --> 00:32:39,390
our YouTube channel, ambassadorship,

673
00:32:39,391 --> 00:32:40,826
and the general manager gig.

674
00:32:41,994 --> 00:32:43,994
To celebrate today's showdown,

675
00:32:43,995 --> 00:32:47,865
I put together a special event
as head of PR.

676
00:32:48,033 --> 00:32:52,370
Whoever comes up with the catchiest slogan
to hook future team owners...

677
00:32:52,438 --> 00:32:54,639
takes home an exclusive prize.

678
00:32:56,575 --> 00:33:00,745
Let's see what you've got.

679
00:33:00,746 --> 00:33:02,046
(Wonder Dogs over Samsung
and SK Hynix stocks)

680
00:33:02,214 --> 00:33:05,349
"Season 3 bound for V-League!"

681
00:33:07,255 --> 00:33:09,022
"Found the Wonder Dogs."

682
00:33:09,054 --> 00:33:11,055
"Who are you looking at? You're up!"

683
00:33:11,557 --> 00:33:14,860
"Seung Kwan,
you should just buy the team!"

684
00:33:14,861 --> 00:33:16,194
Wait, me?

685
00:33:16,222 --> 00:33:17,622
(Nodding hard)

686
00:33:18,397 --> 00:33:19,130
(Shaking)

687
00:33:19,131 --> 00:33:20,632
My hands are literally trembling.

688
00:33:21,633 --> 00:33:24,268
(Meanwhile)

689
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:31,174
(Today's rivals roll in.)

690
00:33:35,614 --> 00:33:36,957
(Pyo Seung Ju, No. 19, outside hitter)

691
00:33:36,982 --> 00:33:38,583
(Former Wonder Dog,
current Pink Spiders outside hitter)

692
00:33:39,051 --> 00:33:39,939
(Lee Na Yeon, No. 33, setter)

693
00:33:39,963 --> 00:33:41,686
(Former Wonder Dog,
current Pink Spiders setter)

694
00:33:42,154 --> 00:33:45,289
(The visiting squad steps into the arena.)

695
00:33:46,392 --> 00:33:48,827
- Hello.
- Hello.

696
00:33:48,828 --> 00:33:51,062
- Good to see you.
- Hello.

697
00:33:51,263 --> 00:33:52,831
Did you guys dial in your prep?

698
00:33:53,098 --> 00:33:54,866
The second this match hit the schedule,

699
00:33:54,867 --> 00:33:56,568
all I could think about was last year.

700
00:33:56,902 --> 00:33:59,637
I promised myself
we're taking it this time.

701
00:33:59,638 --> 00:34:01,440
You've got that look in your eye today.

702
00:34:01,441 --> 00:34:02,840
I didn't come here to mess around.

703
00:34:02,841 --> 00:34:04,910
Your opening lineup is loaded.

704
00:34:04,911 --> 00:34:06,578
This won't be a walk in the park.

705
00:34:07,346 --> 00:34:09,314
Are both the former Wonder Dogs starting?

706
00:34:10,215 --> 00:34:12,983
You'll see right away that both of them...

707
00:34:12,984 --> 00:34:14,318
came locked and loaded.

708
00:34:14,319 --> 00:34:16,053
Their mentality heading into this match...

709
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:19,723
As Season One alumni,
Na Yeon and Seung Ju...

710
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:21,960
have a point to prove
against the Season Two roster.

711
00:34:22,661 --> 00:34:25,595
I've got a read
on Seung Ju and Na Yeon already.

712
00:34:25,596 --> 00:34:27,498
You must know their tendencies inside out.

713
00:34:27,499 --> 00:34:30,569
We spent hours scheming
specifically for them.

714
00:34:30,570 --> 00:34:34,229
My personal goal is
to keep Seung Ju in single digits.

715
00:34:34,254 --> 00:34:35,672
You're locking her down completely?

716
00:34:35,674 --> 00:34:38,876
I'm sure going to try.

717
00:34:38,901 --> 00:34:42,537
That's pretty much the plan.

718
00:34:43,383 --> 00:34:46,290
(Meanwhile, the arena hits a fever pitch.)

719
00:34:46,618 --> 00:34:50,087
Let's go, Wonder Dogs!

720
00:34:50,789 --> 00:34:52,189
(Nods)

721
00:34:54,598 --> 00:34:55,427
They're here.

722
00:34:57,329 --> 00:34:58,496
Hello.

723
00:35:03,695 --> 00:35:05,664
(Glancing)

724
00:35:07,205 --> 00:35:09,804
Their uniforms have changed a bit,
haven't they?

725
00:35:09,805 --> 00:35:11,305
They look totally different.

726
00:35:35,053 --> 00:35:37,320
We were with the Wonder Dogs last year.

727
00:35:37,687 --> 00:35:40,186
Now that we're back in the V-League,

728
00:35:40,187 --> 00:35:42,453
I think our team can win.

729
00:35:43,020 --> 00:35:46,350
I think the most important thing is...

730
00:35:46,351 --> 00:35:49,353
doing your best in your own position.

731
00:35:49,953 --> 00:35:51,920
I'll show you how we win.

732
00:35:54,287 --> 00:35:56,752
The Wonder Dogs started
the season with a hard-won victory.

733
00:35:56,753 --> 00:35:58,686
Now, they aim for consecutive wins...

734
00:35:58,687 --> 00:36:00,352
against the Pink Spiders,
their familiar rivals.

735
00:36:00,353 --> 00:36:02,186
It's the Wonder Dogs
versus the Pink Spiders.

736
00:36:02,187 --> 00:36:04,352
I'll be joined
by commentator Yang Hyo Jin.

737
00:36:04,353 --> 00:36:06,087
- Hello.
- Hello.

738
00:36:06,487 --> 00:36:10,152
The Wonder Dogs are facing
the Pink Spiders again in Season Two,

739
00:36:10,153 --> 00:36:12,219
their opponents in the final match
of Season One.

740
00:36:12,220 --> 00:36:13,220
Exactly.

741
00:36:14,020 --> 00:36:17,253
(In the final match of Season 1)

742
00:36:17,278 --> 00:36:18,828
Against the Pink Spiders...

743
00:36:18,853 --> 00:36:21,953
(The Wonder Dogs beat them 3 to 0
in a complete shutout.)

744
00:36:22,753 --> 00:36:23,819
Run.

745
00:36:23,820 --> 00:36:27,186
The Pink Spiders probably prepared
even harder for today's match.

746
00:36:27,187 --> 00:36:30,420
They'll be looking for revenge.

747
00:36:31,853 --> 00:36:34,052
And looking at today's starting lineup,

748
00:36:34,053 --> 00:36:36,541
- they've got a lot of strong players.
- Exactly.

749
00:36:36,575 --> 00:36:38,255
Kim Da Eun is also getting ready to play.

750
00:36:38,385 --> 00:36:39,417
(Outside hitter Kim Da Eun)

751
00:36:39,418 --> 00:36:42,417
The starting lineup is
packed with first-stringers today.

752
00:36:42,418 --> 00:36:43,285
Exactly.

753
00:36:43,286 --> 00:36:45,084
(Outside hitter Choi Eun Ji)

754
00:36:45,085 --> 00:36:47,117
As the most successful team
in V-League history,

755
00:36:47,118 --> 00:36:48,884
they're going to be tough opponents today.

756
00:36:48,885 --> 00:36:49,984
I think so.

757
00:36:49,985 --> 00:36:53,250
The biggest change is that some players
who used to be on our side,

758
00:36:53,251 --> 00:36:56,750
the Wonder Dogs' key players,
Pyo Seung Ju and Lee Na Yeon,

759
00:36:56,751 --> 00:36:59,850
- are now playing against us.
- That's right.

760
00:36:59,851 --> 00:37:03,984
They must know the Wonder Dogs'
strengths and weaknesses very well.

761
00:37:03,985 --> 00:37:04,818
Absolutely.

762
00:37:05,351 --> 00:37:08,117
I'm really looking forward to seeing...

763
00:37:08,118 --> 00:37:09,284
how these two perform today.

764
00:37:09,285 --> 00:37:10,185
Right.

765
00:37:10,485 --> 00:37:13,384
On the other hand, there's a player
who came to the Wonder Dogs,

766
00:37:13,385 --> 00:37:14,950
from the Pink Spiders.

767
00:37:14,951 --> 00:37:18,117
That's right. Setter Kim Da Sol spent...

768
00:37:18,118 --> 00:37:20,417
thirteen years with the Pink Spiders.

769
00:37:20,418 --> 00:37:22,891
Right, so I imagine she'll be
extra determined today.

770
00:37:22,921 --> 00:37:26,097
(Facing her former team as an opponent)

771
00:37:30,902 --> 00:37:33,402
Now that I'm with the Wonder Dogs,

772
00:37:33,702 --> 00:37:35,601
it feels a little unfamiliar.

773
00:37:35,602 --> 00:37:37,368
A lot of thoughts are
going through my mind.

774
00:37:37,769 --> 00:37:41,835
It just makes me want to do even better.

775
00:37:43,035 --> 00:37:44,901
Da Eun, I'll hit one back-row attack.

776
00:37:44,902 --> 00:37:46,302
Na Yeon, I'll handle the ones here.

777
00:37:51,702 --> 00:37:53,268
Should I set it a bit lower?

778
00:37:53,269 --> 00:37:54,769
Yes, set it a little lower.

779
00:37:56,469 --> 00:37:58,802
(Attempting it again right away)

780
00:37:58,969 --> 00:38:00,068
This is actually better.

781
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:01,102
You think this is better?

782
00:38:01,402 --> 00:38:02,569
Set it to me again.

783
00:38:07,402 --> 00:38:09,135
(Finally got the timing right)

784
00:38:10,002 --> 00:38:10,969
Set it to me again.

785
00:38:17,102 --> 00:38:18,402
Nice set.

786
00:38:20,735 --> 00:38:23,369
I could already see it
during their warm-up.

787
00:38:23,769 --> 00:38:26,002
The chemistry between those two...

788
00:38:26,635 --> 00:38:28,435
It's a little intimidating.

789
00:38:30,102 --> 00:38:33,168
They've come here determined to win,
no matter what.

790
00:38:33,169 --> 00:38:36,069
I could see how fired up they were.

791
00:38:36,502 --> 00:38:38,435
I was a little worried, but...

792
00:38:38,869 --> 00:38:43,135
If we trust our game plan
and execute it well,

793
00:38:44,469 --> 00:38:45,635
we should win.

794
00:38:50,235 --> 00:38:52,135
They're playing
in front of a live crowd today.

795
00:38:52,735 --> 00:38:54,969
In front of 2,000 spectators,

796
00:38:55,535 --> 00:38:58,102
it's a showdown between the ex-Wonder Dogs
Pyo Seung Ju and Lee Na Yeon,

797
00:38:58,802 --> 00:39:00,734
and today's new Wonder Dogs.

798
00:39:00,735 --> 00:39:01,669
That's right.

799
00:39:03,369 --> 00:39:05,469
We know Seung Ju's and Na Yeon's...

800
00:39:06,035 --> 00:39:08,969
strengths and weaknesses inside and out.

801
00:39:10,402 --> 00:39:11,769
This will be an easy game for us.

802
00:39:12,702 --> 00:39:13,869
It should be fun.

803
00:39:19,902 --> 00:39:22,234
Let's check
the Wonder Dogs' starting lineup.

804
00:39:22,235 --> 00:39:24,668
Zone One, setter Ha Hyo Rim.

805
00:39:24,669 --> 00:39:26,502
Outside hitter, Enkhsoyol.

806
00:39:26,916 --> 00:39:28,769
Middle blocker, Lee Ho Bin.

807
00:39:29,107 --> 00:39:31,202
Opposite spiker, Yoon Young In.

808
00:39:31,702 --> 00:39:33,635
Outside hitter, Back Chae Rim.

809
00:39:34,235 --> 00:39:36,002
Middle blocker, Kim Bo Been.

810
00:39:36,435 --> 00:39:38,502
And liberos, Chae Seon Ah
and Seo Yu Kyung.

811
00:39:42,769 --> 00:39:44,934
Let's check
the Pink Spiders' starting lineup.

812
00:39:44,935 --> 00:39:45,968
In Zone One,

813
00:39:45,969 --> 00:39:47,468
setter Lee Na Yeon.

814
00:39:47,469 --> 00:39:49,302
Outside hitter, Pyo Seung Ju.

815
00:39:49,735 --> 00:39:51,502
Middle blocker, Lim Hye Rim.

816
00:39:52,069 --> 00:39:53,869
Opposite spiker, Kim Da Eun.

817
00:39:54,369 --> 00:39:56,235
Outside hitter, Choi Eun Ji.

818
00:39:56,869 --> 00:39:58,901
Middle blocker, Pyeon Ji Su.

819
00:39:58,902 --> 00:40:00,469
And Libero, Park Su Yeon.

820
00:40:06,735 --> 00:40:08,102
At the beginning,

821
00:40:08,535 --> 00:40:10,702
target Zone One with our serves.

822
00:40:11,102 --> 00:40:12,834
Keep working together.

823
00:40:12,835 --> 00:40:14,468
- Don't forget, okay?
- Okay.

824
00:40:14,469 --> 00:40:17,701
When Ji Su goes for a quick attack,
stay on the line.

825
00:40:17,702 --> 00:40:20,934
When Hye Rim sets a quick ball
to the middle, cover Zone Five.

826
00:40:20,935 --> 00:40:21,835
Got that?

827
00:40:21,836 --> 00:40:23,568
(Reviewing defensive strategies
for each opponent)

828
00:40:23,569 --> 00:40:25,731
Seung Ju, drop back on defense
before the attack comes.

829
00:40:26,135 --> 00:40:27,801
Let's get going, right from the start.

830
00:40:27,802 --> 00:40:29,534
(Take control from the very beginning.)

831
00:40:29,535 --> 00:40:31,835
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

832
00:40:35,435 --> 00:40:37,502
- Let's get together and cheer.
- Okay.

833
00:40:38,902 --> 00:40:40,801
When serving and receiving
early in the game,

834
00:40:40,802 --> 00:40:42,668
stay focused and take your time.

835
00:40:42,669 --> 00:40:43,535
Okay.

836
00:40:43,835 --> 00:40:45,901
And to our middles...

837
00:40:45,902 --> 00:40:48,802
If they play fast,
our blockers might be a little late.

838
00:40:49,102 --> 00:40:49,969
So don't follow.

839
00:40:49,970 --> 00:40:51,769
We'll cover the gaps on defense.

840
00:40:52,069 --> 00:40:54,534
Young In has a shot where she turns
the ball at the last moment.

841
00:40:54,535 --> 00:40:56,934
Make sure you watch it
all the way through.

842
00:40:56,935 --> 00:40:58,202
Let's keep our line.

843
00:40:58,935 --> 00:41:03,402
(The Pink Spiders have
a Wonder Dogs expert on their side too.)

844
00:41:08,169 --> 00:41:09,602
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

845
00:41:11,035 --> 00:41:12,569
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

846
00:41:13,502 --> 00:41:16,169
(Lee Na Yeon)

847
00:41:16,635 --> 00:41:18,568
The setter is in Zone One.

848
00:41:18,569 --> 00:41:20,334
Just as we expected.

849
00:41:20,335 --> 00:41:21,535
Switch over there.

850
00:41:21,735 --> 00:41:22,768
(Just as planned)

851
00:41:22,769 --> 00:41:24,201
I'll cover the right side.

852
00:41:24,202 --> 00:41:25,969
Oh, no.

853
00:41:26,169 --> 00:41:27,869
Move to the left.

854
00:41:28,069 --> 00:41:29,468
To the left, now.

855
00:41:29,469 --> 00:41:30,735
(Moving over)

856
00:41:31,202 --> 00:41:33,835
They've pulled over this way.

857
00:41:34,135 --> 00:41:35,368
Go to the net.

858
00:41:35,369 --> 00:41:36,235
Zone One.

859
00:41:36,235 --> 00:41:37,135
Watch Zone One.

860
00:41:37,136 --> 00:41:39,702
(Reading the formation
and sizing each other up)

861
00:41:40,769 --> 00:41:41,835
I got it.

862
00:41:42,769 --> 00:41:46,035
(A fierce battle of wits
even before the match begins)

863
00:41:46,302 --> 00:41:48,969
Let's make it 1 to 0, Wonder Dogs!

864
00:41:49,469 --> 00:41:51,218
They haven't done that in eight matches.

865
00:41:52,002 --> 00:41:54,735
Not even once across Seasons 1 and 2.

866
00:41:56,202 --> 00:41:57,934
The first set begins
with Ha Hyo Rim serving.

867
00:41:57,935 --> 00:41:58,902
Set One starts now.

868
00:41:59,102 --> 00:42:03,234
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

869
00:42:03,235 --> 00:42:05,902
- Let's go.
- Boom.

870
00:42:07,084 --> 00:42:07,858
(Set by Lee Na Yeon)

871
00:42:07,865 --> 00:42:08,668
Lee Na Yeon.

872
00:42:08,902 --> 00:42:10,002
(Seung Ju attacks.)

873
00:42:10,335 --> 00:42:11,302
A tip by Pyo Seung Ju.

874
00:42:11,869 --> 00:42:12,735
It's kept alive.

875
00:42:13,535 --> 00:42:14,469
It's going up.

876
00:42:14,470 --> 00:42:15,868
(Determined to score
the first point today)

877
00:42:15,869 --> 00:42:18,068
A powerful hit!

878
00:42:18,069 --> 00:42:20,535
(First set, Pink Spiders 0
: Wonder Dogs 1)

879
00:42:20,969 --> 00:42:22,634
Great job.

880
00:42:22,635 --> 00:42:26,002
Enkhsoyol scores the first point!

881
00:42:26,702 --> 00:42:28,634
Enkhsoyol!

882
00:42:28,635 --> 00:42:29,869
- Enkhsoyol.
- Enkhsoyol.

883
00:42:32,435 --> 00:42:34,335
I can't believe it.

884
00:42:34,735 --> 00:42:37,934
Ever since I started commentating
on the Wonder Dogs,

885
00:42:37,935 --> 00:42:39,501
this is the first time
they've scored the opening point.

886
00:42:39,502 --> 00:42:42,869
Finally, they got the first point.

887
00:42:43,435 --> 00:42:46,868
It shouldn't have been
this hard to get a point.

888
00:42:46,869 --> 00:42:48,501
They're off to a great start today.

889
00:42:48,502 --> 00:42:49,435
Definitely.

890
00:42:50,069 --> 00:42:51,168
After a whole year...

891
00:42:51,169 --> 00:42:52,768
(Seung Ju's attack fails.)

892
00:42:52,769 --> 00:42:55,834
(They must keep pushing forward.)

893
00:42:55,835 --> 00:42:58,168
Don't serve to Zone Six.

894
00:42:58,169 --> 00:43:00,169
Go for Zone One.

895
00:43:00,802 --> 00:43:03,869
(The serve's target)

896
00:43:04,135 --> 00:43:06,535
(Starting to target Lee Na Yeon)

897
00:43:06,669 --> 00:43:09,569
- Let's go. Boom.
- Let's go. Boom.

898
00:43:09,902 --> 00:43:11,001
She's shaken.

899
00:43:11,002 --> 00:43:12,502
Now is the time.

900
00:43:13,769 --> 00:43:14,291
Lee Na Yeon.

901
00:43:14,292 --> 00:43:15,469
(As expected, the set goes to the left.)

902
00:43:16,335 --> 00:43:17,335
Pyo Seung Ju gets the ball again.

903
00:43:17,336 --> 00:43:18,701
It's too low!

904
00:43:18,702 --> 00:43:19,702
(The ball didn't clear the net.)

905
00:43:19,703 --> 00:43:21,534
(What great luck!)

906
00:43:21,535 --> 00:43:22,469
That's a point.

907
00:43:23,235 --> 00:43:25,935
(The strategy of targeting
Na Yeon pays off.)

908
00:43:26,235 --> 00:43:27,801
(Why is this taking so long?)

909
00:43:27,802 --> 00:43:29,850
They weren't quite in sync.

910
00:43:29,881 --> 00:43:31,381
Sorry, that was my fault.

911
00:43:31,602 --> 00:43:34,434
That's okay. Take your time.

912
00:43:34,435 --> 00:43:37,235
(If you put pressure on Na Yeon,)

913
00:43:37,928 --> 00:43:38,858
(Seung Ju shuts down too.)

914
00:43:38,882 --> 00:43:41,601
They need to keep disrupting
their reception just like that.

915
00:43:41,602 --> 00:43:46,568
Right now, Lee Na Yeon and Pyo Seung Ju
are receiving almost every serve.

916
00:43:46,569 --> 00:43:47,369
Exactly.

917
00:43:48,002 --> 00:43:49,101
They seem a little nervous.

918
00:43:49,102 --> 00:43:50,835
- And it's understandable.
- I know.

919
00:43:51,102 --> 00:43:52,202
The score is 2 to 0.

920
00:43:52,935 --> 00:43:54,701
Seung Ju isn't having
a great day so far. Good.

921
00:43:54,702 --> 00:43:56,802
More.

922
00:43:57,102 --> 00:43:58,702
Move more toward Zone One.

923
00:43:59,269 --> 00:44:03,769
(Going after Na Yeon once more)

924
00:44:05,069 --> 00:44:07,669
(Na Yeon is the target.)

925
00:44:08,102 --> 00:44:10,234
(The hunt is on.)

926
00:44:10,235 --> 00:44:11,102
Hyo Rim serves.

927
00:44:11,669 --> 00:44:13,002
- Their reception is off.
- That's it.

928
00:44:14,369 --> 00:44:15,468
Lee Na Yeon.

929
00:44:15,469 --> 00:44:17,130
As expected, to the middle.

930
00:44:17,669 --> 00:44:19,068
- Hit it.
- Here it comes again.

931
00:44:19,069 --> 00:44:19,902
Here it comes.

932
00:44:20,535 --> 00:44:22,334
They keep it alive
and set it to the back row.

933
00:44:22,335 --> 00:44:23,273
Spike.

934
00:44:23,294 --> 00:44:24,310
(Out)

935
00:44:24,335 --> 00:44:25,569
It's out.

936
00:44:25,902 --> 00:44:27,734
(Oh, no.)

937
00:44:27,735 --> 00:44:29,102
(What a shame.)

938
00:44:31,302 --> 00:44:34,235
The former captain of the Wonder Dogs,
Pyo Seung Ju, steps up to serve.

939
00:44:38,435 --> 00:44:42,302
(The former captain
who once led the Wonder Dogs)

940
00:44:44,802 --> 00:44:46,668
The score is 2 to 1.
Pyo Seung Ju is serving.

941
00:44:46,669 --> 00:44:47,702
(Now she is on the other team.)

942
00:44:48,569 --> 00:44:50,701
It felt strange,

943
00:44:50,702 --> 00:44:52,169
kind of unsettling.

944
00:44:52,969 --> 00:44:55,069
It's going to dip.

945
00:44:57,022 --> 00:45:00,091
It feels strange facing them as opponents,

946
00:45:01,460 --> 00:45:03,060
but we can't lose.

947
00:45:04,296 --> 00:45:06,731
(Targeted serve instructions)

948
00:45:06,732 --> 00:45:07,732
I'll take it.

949
00:45:07,733 --> 00:45:10,168
(Target: Enkhsoyol)

950
00:45:10,169 --> 00:45:11,102
Let's get it!

951
00:45:12,704 --> 00:45:13,637
Just one point.

952
00:45:16,408 --> 00:45:17,942
Mine!

953
00:45:18,009 --> 00:45:18,842
(The serve hits Enkhsoyol.)

954
00:45:18,843 --> 00:45:19,743
That was a shaky reception.

955
00:45:19,744 --> 00:45:20,744
A high ball!

956
00:45:21,079 --> 00:45:22,212
- Cover!
- Hit it!

957
00:45:22,213 --> 00:45:23,647
They send it high into the air.
Young In hits.

958
00:45:24,182 --> 00:45:25,315
She gets it over.

959
00:45:25,717 --> 00:45:26,750
Hit it!

960
00:45:27,519 --> 00:45:28,519
Too high!

961
00:45:29,588 --> 00:45:30,421
Hey!

962
00:45:30,422 --> 00:45:31,255
A jump set.

963
00:45:33,525 --> 00:45:34,758
A powerful spike to the opposite side!

964
00:45:34,759 --> 00:45:36,060
(In bounds)

965
00:45:36,061 --> 00:45:38,162
It lands inside the line.

966
00:45:38,397 --> 00:45:40,210
(Da Eun scores!)

967
00:45:41,600 --> 00:45:42,967
- Good.
- Nice job.

968
00:45:42,968 --> 00:45:44,335
Nice set.

969
00:45:44,936 --> 00:45:45,770
Well done.

970
00:45:45,771 --> 00:45:48,605
It was 2 to 0, but now it's tied at 2.

971
00:45:50,609 --> 00:45:52,176
(Targeted serve instructions)

972
00:45:52,277 --> 00:45:55,446
- Everyone, watch for the short serve!
- Call for it if it's yours.

973
00:45:55,580 --> 00:45:57,681
Watch for the ones that drop sharply.

974
00:45:57,949 --> 00:45:59,883
- Here we go!
- Yes!

975
00:45:59,884 --> 00:46:01,318
(We'll score again.)

976
00:46:01,319 --> 00:46:02,920
Seung Ju serves again.

977
00:46:05,224 --> 00:46:06,056
Mine!

978
00:46:06,425 --> 00:46:07,925
Enkhsoyol struggles
with the reception again.

979
00:46:08,460 --> 00:46:09,794
- Hit it!
- Enkhsoyol.

980
00:46:10,095 --> 00:46:11,529
Seung Ju digs it up from the backcourt.

981
00:46:11,530 --> 00:46:12,363
Darn it.

982
00:46:12,565 --> 00:46:14,432
Cover it! Get in there!

983
00:46:15,433 --> 00:46:16,867
(The team moves
under Seung Ju's direction.)

984
00:46:16,868 --> 00:46:17,768
To the right!

985
00:46:18,270 --> 00:46:20,005
And they score.

986
00:46:20,006 --> 00:46:23,741
Let's slow it down just a little.
Our blocking looks good right now.

987
00:46:24,176 --> 00:46:25,543
Yes!

988
00:46:25,544 --> 00:46:26,744
(First set, Pink Spiders 4
: Wonder Dogs 3)

989
00:46:26,745 --> 00:46:27,812
They're relentless.

990
00:46:28,013 --> 00:46:30,481
They keep targeting Enkhsoyol
with their serves.

991
00:46:30,482 --> 00:46:32,283
That was my mistake!

992
00:46:34,086 --> 00:46:35,186
Is Zone One okay?

993
00:46:37,289 --> 00:46:38,723
Let's go!

994
00:46:38,957 --> 00:46:40,223
The score is 3 to 4 now.

995
00:46:40,224 --> 00:46:41,458
- Get into position!
- Let's go!

996
00:46:44,162 --> 00:46:45,028
In 1, 2!

997
00:46:47,032 --> 00:46:48,766
(Is it going over?)

998
00:46:49,201 --> 00:46:50,168
Over!

999
00:46:50,569 --> 00:46:51,502
It passes over!

1000
00:46:51,503 --> 00:46:52,503
(Direct kill)

1001
00:46:52,504 --> 00:46:53,337
Hey!

1002
00:46:53,538 --> 00:46:55,072
- Hey!
- Nice, Na Yeon.

1003
00:46:55,073 --> 00:46:56,039
(Good job.)

1004
00:46:56,040 --> 00:46:59,109
Set it closer to the net.
How far are you planning to push it?

1005
00:46:59,379 --> 00:47:01,245
The Pink Spiders...

1006
00:47:01,246 --> 00:47:03,948
keep targeting Enkhsoyol
with their serves.

1007
00:47:03,949 --> 00:47:05,183
Yes, I think...

1008
00:47:05,550 --> 00:47:07,184
they'll keep putting pressure
on Enkhsoyol...

1009
00:47:07,185 --> 00:47:10,120
until the very end of the match.

1010
00:47:10,289 --> 00:47:13,090
She'll have to find a way
to handle that pressure.

1011
00:47:13,091 --> 00:47:14,625
- That's right.
- Enkhsoyol!

1012
00:47:14,626 --> 00:47:15,827
(Enkhsoyol is the target once again.)

1013
00:47:15,828 --> 00:47:17,228
The score is now 3 to 5.

1014
00:47:19,297 --> 00:47:20,897
- Enkhsoyol again.
- Get it!

1015
00:47:20,898 --> 00:47:21,865
A back set!

1016
00:47:21,866 --> 00:47:23,300
Young In gets blocked!

1017
00:47:23,869 --> 00:47:26,838
- Where are you even hitting the ball?
- We need to turn it around!

1018
00:47:26,839 --> 00:47:29,740
Ultimately, if Young In can't
break through,

1019
00:47:30,008 --> 00:47:33,610
the pressure falls on the other players.

1020
00:47:33,611 --> 00:47:34,544
That's right.

1021
00:47:34,545 --> 00:47:36,880
Watch her blocking a little more closely.
Don't let Young In hit it down the line.

1022
00:47:37,782 --> 00:47:40,450
Keep forcing her to hit deep.

1023
00:47:40,886 --> 00:47:43,153
If she moves back
and tries to hit down the line,

1024
00:47:43,154 --> 00:47:44,321
you can block her.

1025
00:47:44,689 --> 00:47:45,756
Young In!

1026
00:47:47,425 --> 00:47:50,160
She'll fake the line
and then go cross-court.

1027
00:47:50,161 --> 00:47:51,294
So do the opposite.

1028
00:47:51,295 --> 00:47:53,597
(Using that against them
to hit down the line)

1029
00:47:55,534 --> 00:47:56,400
In 1, 2!

1030
00:47:56,835 --> 00:47:57,668
Mine!

1031
00:47:57,669 --> 00:47:58,602
Enkhsoyol receives.

1032
00:47:58,603 --> 00:47:59,703
Set it back.

1033
00:47:59,704 --> 00:48:01,806
(She goes down the line!)

1034
00:48:01,807 --> 00:48:02,673
They set it up again.

1035
00:48:02,980 --> 00:48:04,880
- Young In attacks. That's it.
- Nice.

1036
00:48:05,544 --> 00:48:06,911
(Exactly as predicted)

1037
00:48:06,912 --> 00:48:08,679
That's it. See? That's how she hits.

1038
00:48:10,282 --> 00:48:12,383
Look at that one too.
Who served just now?

1039
00:48:12,384 --> 00:48:13,484
- Right?
- Yes.

1040
00:48:13,485 --> 00:48:16,621
You can really tell how well
these teams know each other.

1041
00:48:16,622 --> 00:48:18,890
They anticipate each other's moves
and use that knowledge...

1042
00:48:18,915 --> 00:48:19,936
- to counter each other.
- Right.

1043
00:48:20,091 --> 00:48:21,558
(Glancing)

1044
00:48:22,627 --> 00:48:23,527
Chae Rim.

1045
00:48:23,528 --> 00:48:24,394
(Chae Rim, over there.)

1046
00:48:24,989 --> 00:48:27,657
Enkhsoyol, Na Yeon is
in front of you this time.

1047
00:48:27,718 --> 00:48:29,499
(Na Yeon must be the blocker.)

1048
00:48:30,068 --> 00:48:32,069
Keep the setter in place!

1049
00:48:33,071 --> 00:48:35,739
Na Yeon is a shorter blocker,
so we need to score...

1050
00:48:36,308 --> 00:48:38,109
as many points as possible
when we attack against her.

1051
00:48:38,543 --> 00:48:39,576
We're going to keep...

1052
00:48:39,911 --> 00:48:42,913
at it relentlessly until it works.

1053
00:48:44,783 --> 00:48:46,050
Young In serves.

1054
00:48:46,051 --> 00:48:47,518
(Young In serves.)

1055
00:48:51,022 --> 00:48:52,322
- Ji Su!
- A slide attack!

1056
00:48:52,624 --> 00:48:53,724
Go for it!

1057
00:48:53,825 --> 00:48:54,958
- Great dig.
- Send it over!

1058
00:48:55,093 --> 00:48:56,326
Handle it!

1059
00:48:56,327 --> 00:48:57,695
They send it over. They can't let it drop!

1060
00:48:57,696 --> 00:48:59,363
Good!

1061
00:48:59,497 --> 00:49:00,664
Again!

1062
00:49:00,665 --> 00:49:01,765
Hit it!

1063
00:49:01,867 --> 00:49:03,500
(The real target is right here.)

1064
00:49:03,802 --> 00:49:05,669
- A quick change! Yu Kyung with the dig!
- Mine!

1065
00:49:05,804 --> 00:49:07,538
That's it. Let's go.

1066
00:49:07,906 --> 00:49:08,772
Set it up!

1067
00:49:09,140 --> 00:49:10,540
(They're coming!)

1068
00:49:11,710 --> 00:49:12,877
- Hit it!
- To Chae Rim!

1069
00:49:12,878 --> 00:49:13,978
A spike to the opposite side!

1070
00:49:14,379 --> 00:49:15,813
(Blocked)

1071
00:49:16,047 --> 00:49:16,847
They send it over.

1072
00:49:16,848 --> 00:49:17,648
(Na Yeon's pass feint)

1073
00:49:17,649 --> 00:49:18,649
They read it perfectly!

1074
00:49:18,650 --> 00:49:19,716
(I shouldn't have done that.)

1075
00:49:19,717 --> 00:49:20,684
Go deep!

1076
00:49:20,685 --> 00:49:21,518
Again!

1077
00:49:22,654 --> 00:49:24,588
- Hit it!
- Hold it!

1078
00:49:25,023 --> 00:49:26,190
Take it slow!

1079
00:49:27,325 --> 00:49:28,825
Another spike!

1080
00:49:28,826 --> 00:49:29,993
(It breaks through!)

1081
00:49:30,862 --> 00:49:31,695
(Sorry.)

1082
00:49:33,298 --> 00:49:34,365
That's it!

1083
00:49:34,366 --> 00:49:38,036
(Relentlessly targeting
Na Yeon finally pays off!)

1084
00:49:38,037 --> 00:49:40,271
- Good!
- Nice defense!

1085
00:49:40,272 --> 00:49:43,173
Once again, they kept targeting Na Yeon...

1086
00:49:43,174 --> 00:49:44,241
until they broke through her block.

1087
00:49:44,542 --> 00:49:47,878
Coach Kim relentlessly exploited
their weakness.

1088
00:49:48,713 --> 00:49:50,281
It's an intense battle
right at the start of the first set.

1089
00:49:50,282 --> 00:49:53,350
It is only possible because both teams
know exactly how to hurt each other.

1090
00:49:53,351 --> 00:49:54,484
That's right.

1091
00:49:57,722 --> 00:49:59,456
That's too weak. Target Zone One.

1092
00:49:59,457 --> 00:50:02,493
Coach Kim tells Young In
where to aim her serve.

1093
00:50:02,494 --> 00:50:03,360
Right.

1094
00:50:03,928 --> 00:50:05,161
(The targeted serve hits its mark.)

1095
00:50:05,162 --> 00:50:06,162
Na Yeon.

1096
00:50:06,163 --> 00:50:07,231
(As expected, the set goes to the left.)

1097
00:50:07,232 --> 00:50:08,198
That's it.

1098
00:50:09,567 --> 00:50:10,433
Eun Ji.

1099
00:50:10,434 --> 00:50:11,301
(A block touch)

1100
00:50:11,936 --> 00:50:12,903
They keep it alive.

1101
00:50:12,904 --> 00:50:14,771
Get it! Quickly!

1102
00:50:14,939 --> 00:50:16,273
That's it!

1103
00:50:17,809 --> 00:50:18,776
Hit it!

1104
00:50:18,777 --> 00:50:19,510
(On the hunt again)

1105
00:50:21,680 --> 00:50:24,548
Spike and she scores!

1106
00:50:25,116 --> 00:50:26,349
That's it!

1107
00:50:28,186 --> 00:50:30,554
That was amazing!

1108
00:50:30,555 --> 00:50:31,488
Well done.

1109
00:50:32,891 --> 00:50:33,858
Nice job!

1110
00:50:36,494 --> 00:50:38,929
That was an incredibly sharp attack.

1111
00:50:38,930 --> 00:50:40,931
They're executing the attacks really well.

1112
00:50:40,932 --> 00:50:42,299
(A powerful spike deep into the court)

1113
00:50:42,300 --> 00:50:43,266
- Good!
- Great!

1114
00:50:44,969 --> 00:50:45,936
Sorry about that defense.

1115
00:50:46,338 --> 00:50:48,772
It's okay. We can turn it around.

1116
00:50:54,279 --> 00:50:56,181
Eun Ji, after you receive, push forward.

1117
00:50:56,182 --> 00:50:57,481
She's going to set it back,
so push forward.

1118
00:51:00,318 --> 00:51:01,451
Bo Been!

1119
00:51:01,820 --> 00:51:03,721
I told you to run
when we have two attackers!

1120
00:51:03,722 --> 00:51:05,356
Run!

1121
00:51:12,864 --> 00:51:13,664
Mine!

1122
00:51:13,998 --> 00:51:14,831
It's ours!

1123
00:51:15,167 --> 00:51:15,952
To the left.

1124
00:51:15,953 --> 00:51:17,134
(Another set to the left,
just as expected)

1125
00:51:18,241 --> 00:51:19,169
(Hits the net and falls)

1126
00:51:19,170 --> 00:51:20,037
They keep it alive.

1127
00:51:20,305 --> 00:51:21,672
The ball goes back to Chae Rim.

1128
00:51:21,673 --> 00:51:22,373
(Charging straight at the target)

1129
00:51:22,374 --> 00:51:23,741
Go deep! A tip!

1130
00:51:24,042 --> 00:51:24,842
A tip!

1131
00:51:25,443 --> 00:51:26,276
Mine.

1132
00:51:26,277 --> 00:51:26,977
(Complete chaos)

1133
00:51:27,145 --> 00:51:28,278
Hit it!

1134
00:51:29,247 --> 00:51:30,547
The spike is precise!

1135
00:51:30,548 --> 00:51:32,115
Hit it!

1136
00:51:32,116 --> 00:51:33,350
(A free ball)

1137
00:51:33,351 --> 00:51:34,318
That's it!

1138
00:51:34,519 --> 00:51:35,352
It's going to be a tip!

1139
00:51:35,653 --> 00:51:37,387
- Run!
- Bo Been!

1140
00:51:37,388 --> 00:51:38,421
Run!

1141
00:51:39,057 --> 00:51:40,857
It's going in!

1142
00:51:41,092 --> 00:51:43,193
(Perfect execution
of Coach Kim's strategy)

1143
00:51:45,196 --> 00:51:46,930
They score!

1144
00:51:49,234 --> 00:51:49,934
Nice.

1145
00:51:50,402 --> 00:51:51,769
That was it! Nice job!

1146
00:51:52,337 --> 00:51:55,239
The Wonder Dogs seem to be off
to a pretty good start, don't you think?

1147
00:51:55,240 --> 00:51:56,206
They're playing extremely well.

1148
00:51:56,207 --> 00:51:57,374
That was great!

1149
00:51:57,876 --> 00:51:59,109
Nicely done.

1150
00:51:59,110 --> 00:52:02,780
(A reversal, Pink Spiders 7
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1151
00:52:03,782 --> 00:52:04,715
It's okay.

1152
00:52:05,116 --> 00:52:07,518
The Wonder Dogs lead 8 to 7 as we head...

1153
00:52:07,519 --> 00:52:09,953
into the first technical timeout
of Set One.

1154
00:52:10,955 --> 00:52:13,223
Good job, everyone.

1155
00:52:13,892 --> 00:52:16,093
Our back-row attacks were good,

1156
00:52:16,094 --> 00:52:17,862
- and so were our tips.
- Yes, Coach.

1157
00:52:17,863 --> 00:52:20,864
But our serves were a bit weak.
Put some more power into your serves.

1158
00:52:20,865 --> 00:52:22,933
They're targeting Zone One
with their serves anyway,

1159
00:52:22,934 --> 00:52:25,303
so the receivers in Zone One
need to be ready.

1160
00:52:25,304 --> 00:52:26,804
Na Yeon, when you set from Zone One,

1161
00:52:26,805 --> 00:52:27,872
be a bit more gentle with it.

1162
00:52:27,873 --> 00:52:29,707
Your sets are too tight.

1163
00:52:30,008 --> 00:52:31,809
- And slow down.
- We need to take our time.

1164
00:52:31,810 --> 00:52:32,943
(Checking their offense as well)

1165
00:52:32,944 --> 00:52:34,779
And where have they been directing
most of their serves?

1166
00:52:34,780 --> 00:52:36,747
They're targeting Enkhsoyol.

1167
00:52:36,748 --> 00:52:38,783
Since they're targeting Enkhsoyol so much,
you need to cover more ground.

1168
00:52:38,784 --> 00:52:40,784
When the serve comes from that side,
you guys need to shift over more.

1169
00:52:40,785 --> 00:52:41,652
- Okay.
- Got it?

1170
00:52:41,653 --> 00:52:42,453
Yes.

1171
00:52:43,121 --> 00:52:44,955
I think they're
deliberately targeting you.

1172
00:52:44,956 --> 00:52:45,956
So let's rotate.

1173
00:52:46,825 --> 00:52:49,361
If they keep targeting Zone One,

1174
00:52:49,362 --> 00:52:50,795
watch for it and shift over to cover.

1175
00:52:50,796 --> 00:52:52,730
I'll adjust our strategy
depending on how things go.

1176
00:52:53,231 --> 00:52:56,133
Now that they're serving toward Da Eun,

1177
00:52:56,134 --> 00:52:59,269
the Pink Spiders have Su Yeon cover
that area right away.

1178
00:52:59,270 --> 00:53:00,804
Yes, they're already adjusting.

1179
00:53:00,905 --> 00:53:02,772
They definitely seem to have a strategy.

1180
00:53:04,809 --> 00:53:08,111
We just need to swing
the momentum our way!

1181
00:53:09,581 --> 00:53:12,142
I know better than anyone
how desperate they are...

1182
00:53:12,143 --> 00:53:13,817
and how much pressure they're under,

1183
00:53:14,319 --> 00:53:16,854
but I think it's time to put
some pressure on Chae Rim.

1184
00:53:17,589 --> 00:53:18,522
Two are coming!

1185
00:53:19,190 --> 00:53:21,025
I'll keep targeting that side at first.

1186
00:53:21,026 --> 00:53:22,659
We'll stick with that.

1187
00:53:27,398 --> 00:53:29,466
Young In serves to resume the game.

1188
00:53:32,523 --> 00:53:33,717
- Su Yeon with the reception.
- Nice!

1189
00:53:33,718 --> 00:53:34,705
(A targeted serve near Zone 1)

1190
00:53:35,173 --> 00:53:35,906
Go!

1191
00:53:36,040 --> 00:53:38,174
(Will the set go left again?)

1192
00:53:38,175 --> 00:53:40,710
I think it's time to put
some pressure on Chae Rim.

1193
00:53:40,711 --> 00:53:41,544
Go!

1194
00:53:41,545 --> 00:53:42,712
- Set!
- Get it up high!

1195
00:53:42,713 --> 00:53:43,747
Slide! A back slide!

1196
00:53:45,083 --> 00:53:47,151
(A surprise attack
in the opposite direction)

1197
00:53:47,253 --> 00:53:48,051
It's blocked!

1198
00:53:48,052 --> 00:53:49,052
(That was close!)

1199
00:53:49,387 --> 00:53:51,188
Slide! Set it again!

1200
00:53:51,189 --> 00:53:52,055
Watch the line!

1201
00:53:56,528 --> 00:53:58,028
Nice!

1202
00:53:58,029 --> 00:53:59,730
(Ji Su scores with a slide attack!)

1203
00:53:59,731 --> 00:54:01,432
Great.

1204
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:03,801
Great job going for that slide again!

1205
00:54:04,903 --> 00:54:08,039
(Na Yeon turns the tables!)

1206
00:54:08,040 --> 00:54:09,640
- Nice job.
- I saw it, but I lost it.

1207
00:54:09,641 --> 00:54:11,175
It's okay!

1208
00:54:11,910 --> 00:54:13,410
It's tied at 8 to 8.

1209
00:54:14,412 --> 00:54:15,412
Eun Ji serves.

1210
00:54:17,415 --> 00:54:18,682
Chae Rim receives.

1211
00:54:18,683 --> 00:54:19,483
Cover it!

1212
00:54:20,585 --> 00:54:21,318
Go for the tip!

1213
00:54:21,319 --> 00:54:22,185
They keep it up.

1214
00:54:22,387 --> 00:54:23,754
Hit it now!

1215
00:54:23,755 --> 00:54:24,955
A soft tip!

1216
00:54:26,024 --> 00:54:27,858
She sends it over with a tip.

1217
00:54:27,859 --> 00:54:28,959
Where will it go? Here they come again.

1218
00:54:28,960 --> 00:54:29,893
(Jumping up)

1219
00:54:29,894 --> 00:54:30,661
It's a back attack!

1220
00:54:30,995 --> 00:54:31,895
She got it.

1221
00:54:33,364 --> 00:54:34,531
Right side!

1222
00:54:34,699 --> 00:54:35,666
Go back!

1223
00:54:36,434 --> 00:54:37,868
Another set to Ji Su!

1224
00:54:38,870 --> 00:54:41,338
A delayed attack through the middle!
She scores!

1225
00:54:42,073 --> 00:54:45,108
(Na Yeon and Ji Su score
against them again.)

1226
00:54:45,177 --> 00:54:46,643
The score is now 8 to 9.

1227
00:54:46,644 --> 00:54:48,712
(First set, Pink Spiders 9
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1228
00:54:48,713 --> 00:54:51,982
Once Ji Su's slide attack starts working,
she can keep scoring with it.

1229
00:54:52,251 --> 00:54:54,551
Just watch for the setter sending it
through the middle.

1230
00:54:57,982 --> 00:54:59,147
- Set it up!
- A short pass.

1231
00:54:59,148 --> 00:55:01,082
High ball! Get in there!

1232
00:55:01,948 --> 00:55:03,647
She got it with an underhand toss.
Outside.

1233
00:55:03,648 --> 00:55:04,781
- Mine!
- Run!

1234
00:55:04,782 --> 00:55:05,815
She defends.

1235
00:55:06,515 --> 00:55:08,081
She moves, and it hits the net.

1236
00:55:08,082 --> 00:55:09,115
It's a touch out.

1237
00:55:11,782 --> 00:55:12,814
Nice, Ji Su!

1238
00:55:12,815 --> 00:55:14,647
Great job.

1239
00:55:14,648 --> 00:55:15,682
Good!

1240
00:55:20,248 --> 00:55:22,948
Why didn't you move, Hyo Rim?

1241
00:55:23,315 --> 00:55:24,747
Why did you stay still?
Where's the defense?

1242
00:55:24,748 --> 00:55:25,748
Understood!

1243
00:55:29,848 --> 00:55:33,681
Na Yeon is attacking the middle more
than the left today.

1244
00:55:33,682 --> 00:55:38,215
Yes. She's forcing herself
to use the right side.

1245
00:55:38,882 --> 00:55:42,415
(She usually tossed to the left
during the first season.)

1246
00:55:43,048 --> 00:55:46,548
(Today, she's unpredictable.)

1247
00:55:47,582 --> 00:55:51,248
(And Ji Su finishes it off.)

1248
00:55:52,248 --> 00:55:55,815
(A set play they couldn't expect)

1249
00:55:56,882 --> 00:55:59,348
They went all out to prepare for this.

1250
00:56:00,282 --> 00:56:04,582
Na Yeon definitely had a fire in her eyes.

1251
00:56:06,215 --> 00:56:07,882
I thought I needed to rattle her.

1252
00:56:09,548 --> 00:56:10,947
Let's make up ground!

1253
00:56:10,948 --> 00:56:12,315
Let's catch up!

1254
00:56:14,315 --> 00:56:16,748
(They aim...)

1255
00:56:18,215 --> 00:56:20,948
(for Na Yeon in the front row again.)

1256
00:56:21,915 --> 00:56:24,114
Enkhsoyol!

1257
00:56:24,115 --> 00:56:25,148
It's Na Yeon!

1258
00:56:26,015 --> 00:56:28,015
(They target Na Yeon up front.)

1259
00:56:29,048 --> 00:56:30,273
Two points apart.

1260
00:56:30,274 --> 00:56:31,415
(First set, Pink Spiders 11
: Wonder Dogs 9)

1261
00:56:33,115 --> 00:56:34,115
Su Yeon receives.

1262
00:56:35,115 --> 00:56:36,615
(Ji Su again)

1263
00:56:37,015 --> 00:56:38,015
It's a tip!

1264
00:56:39,282 --> 00:56:40,315
The middle again.

1265
00:56:40,515 --> 00:56:41,615
It's up!

1266
00:56:41,915 --> 00:56:43,415
- It's up!
- They dug it up.

1267
00:56:44,048 --> 00:56:45,082
A joust.

1268
00:56:45,548 --> 00:56:46,548
It's kept alive.

1269
00:56:47,782 --> 00:56:50,082
(Targeting Na Yeon with a low block)

1270
00:56:51,748 --> 00:56:53,615
Spike! She scores!

1271
00:56:53,915 --> 00:56:56,048
(Nice!)

1272
00:56:56,482 --> 00:56:58,047
They just need to keep defending.

1273
00:56:58,048 --> 00:56:59,148
You're right.

1274
00:57:00,615 --> 00:57:03,048
(They finally stopped the bleeding.)

1275
00:57:05,048 --> 00:57:07,115
(Hawk eyes activated)

1276
00:57:07,315 --> 00:57:08,515
(Press it.)

1277
00:57:10,348 --> 00:57:12,815
(Calling for a VAR review)

1278
00:57:13,782 --> 00:57:14,815
Why?

1279
00:57:14,915 --> 00:57:15,948
Why?

1280
00:57:18,415 --> 00:57:22,482
He requested a video review
to see if they really got the ball up.

1281
00:57:29,115 --> 00:57:31,148
Oh, dear. It hit the floor first.

1282
00:57:32,282 --> 00:57:34,482
After review,
the dig is ruled unsuccessful.

1283
00:57:35,182 --> 00:57:36,447
The review confirms...

1284
00:57:36,448 --> 00:57:38,681
the dig was unsuccessful.

1285
00:57:38,682 --> 00:57:40,347
(His hawk eyes were spot-on.)

1286
00:57:40,348 --> 00:57:42,215
(First set, Pink Spiders 12
: Wonder Dogs 9)

1287
00:57:42,582 --> 00:57:45,548
(No time to be disappointed.)

1288
00:57:46,882 --> 00:57:47,915
Hyo Rim!

1289
00:57:48,815 --> 00:57:50,081
When there's a free ball,

1290
00:57:50,082 --> 00:57:51,781
- use back A or back B!
- Yes, Coach.

1291
00:57:51,782 --> 00:57:54,047
Don't run. Just play back A
or back B if it's a free ball.

1292
00:57:54,048 --> 00:57:55,248
(Already planning the next move)

1293
00:57:55,882 --> 00:57:57,348
- If it's a free ball?
- Yes.

1294
00:58:00,548 --> 00:58:01,614
(Ji Su serves.)

1295
00:58:01,615 --> 00:58:03,215
It's 9 to 12, three points apart.

1296
00:58:06,415 --> 00:58:07,615
Hyo Rim kept it alive!

1297
00:58:08,082 --> 00:58:09,115
That's it.

1298
00:58:09,982 --> 00:58:11,382
She softly tips it over!

1299
00:58:12,148 --> 00:58:14,215
- Nice!
- Good!

1300
00:58:17,415 --> 00:58:18,782
(They get a point right back.)

1301
00:58:21,948 --> 00:58:24,382
(Thinking)

1302
00:58:29,148 --> 00:58:31,182
(Target spotted)

1303
00:58:31,815 --> 00:58:34,548
Seung Ju, make sure you get in position.

1304
00:58:37,948 --> 00:58:39,914
It's 11 to 13, two points apart.

1305
00:58:39,915 --> 00:58:41,282
(First set, Pink Spiders 13
: Wonder Dogs 11)

1306
00:58:44,215 --> 00:58:45,982
Na Yeon moves a lot and bumps it up.

1307
00:58:46,715 --> 00:58:48,648
- But it's received from the back.
- Inside!

1308
00:58:49,482 --> 00:58:50,482
Young In!

1309
00:58:51,615 --> 00:58:52,648
(Oh no, you don't!)

1310
00:58:53,215 --> 00:58:54,282
A tip from the right!

1311
00:58:54,982 --> 00:58:56,115
It's blocked.

1312
00:58:57,082 --> 00:58:58,314
(Seung Ju blocked the attack.)

1313
00:58:58,315 --> 00:59:01,048
Their right-side attack needs
to break through.

1314
00:59:01,882 --> 00:59:05,048
(Their block completely shut
Young In down.)

1315
00:59:06,415 --> 00:59:07,847
Why did you finish it like that?

1316
00:59:07,848 --> 00:59:09,047
Toss it over there!

1317
00:59:09,048 --> 00:59:10,281
Yes, Coach.

1318
00:59:10,282 --> 00:59:11,282
(Frustrated)

1319
00:59:13,382 --> 00:59:14,614
(Seung Ju serves again.)

1320
00:59:14,615 --> 00:59:15,915
Seung Ju serves.

1321
00:59:20,015 --> 00:59:22,382
(To Zone 5!)

1322
00:59:23,382 --> 00:59:25,215
(Targeting Enkhsoyol once again)

1323
00:59:28,248 --> 00:59:29,281
(Shaky)

1324
00:59:29,282 --> 00:59:30,547
Okay!

1325
00:59:30,548 --> 00:59:31,548
- A shaky reception.
- Hit it!

1326
00:59:32,448 --> 00:59:33,448
Outside.

1327
00:59:35,615 --> 00:59:37,515
Na Yeon sets a back toss from the middle.

1328
00:59:38,015 --> 00:59:39,048
Right side!

1329
00:59:39,448 --> 00:59:40,515
A touch out.

1330
00:59:43,648 --> 00:59:45,748
Take your time. Keep this up.

1331
00:59:47,215 --> 00:59:49,482
They can't lose any more points now.

1332
00:59:50,982 --> 00:59:52,147
(Seung Ju serves again.)

1333
00:59:52,148 --> 00:59:53,681
It's 11 to 15, four points apart.

1334
00:59:53,682 --> 00:59:55,648
Watch the gap! It's a short ball!

1335
01:00:02,482 --> 01:00:03,548
Mine!

1336
01:00:04,182 --> 01:00:05,848
(The ball is up high.)

1337
01:00:06,248 --> 01:00:07,281
It's over!

1338
01:00:07,282 --> 01:00:08,582
Go! Stay in!

1339
01:00:10,048 --> 01:00:11,048
A direct kill.

1340
01:00:11,715 --> 01:00:12,715
Nice serve!

1341
01:00:13,748 --> 01:00:15,715
Why? What's wrong?

1342
01:00:17,115 --> 01:00:19,081
The gap is widening.

1343
01:00:19,082 --> 01:00:21,248
(A five-point lead in a flash)

1344
01:00:22,282 --> 01:00:26,515
Seung Ju really is determined to win.

1345
01:00:26,915 --> 01:00:28,748
She has a different look in her eyes.

1346
01:00:30,448 --> 01:00:31,515
She digs it up.

1347
01:00:31,915 --> 01:00:33,148
Eun Ji, hit it.

1348
01:00:33,682 --> 01:00:34,682
Eun Ji.

1349
01:00:34,982 --> 01:00:36,247
A block touch out.

1350
01:00:36,248 --> 01:00:37,448
Okay!

1351
01:00:38,948 --> 01:00:40,382
It's 12 to 19.

1352
01:00:40,882 --> 01:00:42,347
Why won't your hands get in there?

1353
01:00:42,348 --> 01:00:44,182
It'll obviously bounce off
if you reach like that!

1354
01:00:44,682 --> 01:00:47,648
It felt like they'd figured us out.

1355
01:00:48,048 --> 01:00:49,582
So they knew after all.

1356
01:00:51,082 --> 01:00:52,482
Mine! Na Yeon!

1357
01:00:52,882 --> 01:00:54,181
Na Yeon's back toss.

1358
01:00:54,182 --> 01:00:55,847
- Cover!
- There's one!

1359
01:00:55,848 --> 01:00:58,081
- Okay! Nice toss!
- Da Eun scores.

1360
01:00:58,082 --> 01:00:59,382
It's 13 to 20.

1361
01:01:00,182 --> 01:01:03,382
I started seeing her
more as a rival than a friend.

1362
01:01:04,282 --> 01:01:06,148
- We need to concentrate more!
- Okay.

1363
01:01:06,482 --> 01:01:07,882
It's okay. One at a time.

1364
01:01:09,448 --> 01:01:10,448
It's fine!

1365
01:01:11,115 --> 01:01:13,982
It's okay! Focus.
We can do this one by one.

1366
01:01:15,148 --> 01:01:16,747
It's all right. Let's take it easy.

1367
01:01:16,748 --> 01:01:18,814
Play with confidence, Myoung Hwa.
I'll cover for you.

1368
01:01:18,815 --> 01:01:20,014
Take it easy.

1369
01:01:20,015 --> 01:01:22,615
- Just hit it. I'll handle the rest.
- Sure.

1370
01:01:23,248 --> 01:01:25,981
Memories of that time suddenly hit me,

1371
01:01:25,982 --> 01:01:27,015
and it felt weird.

1372
01:01:28,215 --> 01:01:29,715
Do it, Su Yeon. Good!

1373
01:01:30,048 --> 01:01:31,148
Hit it!

1374
01:01:33,215 --> 01:01:35,948
The first set is getting harder
and harder.

1375
01:01:36,915 --> 01:01:40,748
(Their former team captain is
now their opponent.)

1376
01:01:41,348 --> 01:01:43,815
I couldn't help but feel so...

1377
01:01:46,548 --> 01:01:47,882
The reception is shaky.

1378
01:01:50,715 --> 01:01:52,281
Ji Su scores an ace.

1379
01:01:52,282 --> 01:01:54,248
(First set, Pink Spiders 23
: Wonder Dogs 15)

1380
01:01:54,415 --> 01:01:56,482
I could see they were getting rattled.

1381
01:01:57,582 --> 01:01:58,747
Whether our rivals are good or not,

1382
01:01:58,748 --> 01:02:02,348
it all comes down
to whether we can pull it off.

1383
01:02:07,482 --> 01:02:09,479
It's the Pink Spiders' set point
in the first set.

1384
01:02:09,480 --> 01:02:10,615
(First set, Pink Spiders 24
: Wonder Dogs 15)

1385
01:02:11,115 --> 01:02:14,247
It looks like Coach Kim has a lot
on her mind.

1386
01:02:14,248 --> 01:02:15,315
Yes.

1387
01:02:16,315 --> 01:02:18,682
(Getting up)

1388
01:02:20,482 --> 01:02:22,348
Set it to Bo Been if the pass is good.

1389
01:02:22,515 --> 01:02:23,715
(Okay.)

1390
01:02:25,382 --> 01:02:26,415
Ji Su serves.

1391
01:02:28,748 --> 01:02:30,247
- Go for it!
- B!

1392
01:02:30,248 --> 01:02:31,282
Da Sol.

1393
01:02:31,415 --> 01:02:32,547
A quick hit from B.

1394
01:02:32,548 --> 01:02:33,614
She scores.

1395
01:02:33,615 --> 01:02:35,148
(Successful attack down the middle)

1396
01:02:35,382 --> 01:02:38,947
Bo Been needs to attack
to keep their offense more diverse.

1397
01:02:38,948 --> 01:02:40,015
Yes, that's right.

1398
01:02:42,715 --> 01:02:44,682
We managed to get a side-out,

1399
01:02:46,648 --> 01:02:49,148
but our serving strategy
didn't really work out,

1400
01:02:51,748 --> 01:02:55,048
so our opponents pulled off
their set plays.

1401
01:02:56,282 --> 01:03:00,282
I figured we wouldn't stand a chance
if we kept hitting that way.

1402
01:03:01,382 --> 01:03:03,448
We had to play to our strengths.

1403
01:03:07,148 --> 01:03:08,748
Bo Been!

1404
01:03:16,048 --> 01:03:17,681
(Instructing to target Zone 2)

1405
01:03:17,682 --> 01:03:18,682
Okay!

1406
01:03:20,248 --> 01:03:21,514
(Changing...)

1407
01:03:21,515 --> 01:03:22,515
(the target zone)

1408
01:03:22,516 --> 01:03:23,647
Serve!

1409
01:03:23,648 --> 01:03:27,615
- Let's go. Boom!
- Let's go. Boom!

1410
01:03:29,682 --> 01:03:30,748
A shaky reception.

1411
01:03:30,882 --> 01:03:31,882
Okay, nice serve.

1412
01:03:31,883 --> 01:03:32,915
Touch. Back toss.

1413
01:03:33,848 --> 01:03:35,115
Min Ji!

1414
01:03:37,548 --> 01:03:38,548
It's out!

1415
01:03:39,182 --> 01:03:41,047
(Forcing an error with a sharp serve)

1416
01:03:41,048 --> 01:03:42,081
Nice!

1417
01:03:42,082 --> 01:03:43,681
Let's go! Keep pushing!

1418
01:03:43,682 --> 01:03:44,748
Take your time.

1419
01:03:45,315 --> 01:03:46,347
It's okay.

1420
01:03:46,348 --> 01:03:48,882
- Why did you hit it into a single block?
- Sorry.

1421
01:03:49,882 --> 01:03:51,448
Calm down.

1422
01:03:52,548 --> 01:03:54,114
They keep losing points.

1423
01:03:54,115 --> 01:03:56,082
We have a good lead, but still.

1424
01:04:01,815 --> 01:04:04,415
(Finding the next target)

1425
01:04:06,948 --> 01:04:08,147
(Targeting Zone 2 again)

1426
01:04:08,148 --> 01:04:09,348
(Nodding)

1427
01:04:11,782 --> 01:04:13,314
(Target zone for the serve)

1428
01:04:13,315 --> 01:04:14,482
It's 17 to 24.

1429
01:04:16,115 --> 01:04:17,115
Bo Been serves.

1430
01:04:18,315 --> 01:04:19,315
(Hits the target)

1431
01:04:19,482 --> 01:04:20,482
It's long!

1432
01:04:20,948 --> 01:04:23,081
That's an error!

1433
01:04:23,082 --> 01:04:26,215
(Touching the net by mistake)

1434
01:04:27,948 --> 01:04:29,247
(The targeted serve leads to an overpass.)

1435
01:04:29,248 --> 01:04:30,315
It's long!

1436
01:04:30,548 --> 01:04:32,248
(It forces an error from the setter.)

1437
01:04:33,382 --> 01:04:37,814
It'd be better if the Wonder Dogs
could build on this momentum.

1438
01:04:37,815 --> 01:04:38,882
(Three points in a row)

1439
01:04:39,948 --> 01:04:41,515
(Cheering)

1440
01:04:45,115 --> 01:04:46,882
Su Yeon!

1441
01:04:47,815 --> 01:04:49,282
They're targeting here.

1442
01:04:53,315 --> 01:04:55,315
(Scanning with his hawk eyes)

1443
01:04:56,393 --> 01:04:58,661
(An eye for an eye)

1444
01:04:59,496 --> 01:05:02,164
(The eagle-eyed coach is laser-focused.)

1445
01:05:03,333 --> 01:05:07,636
(Zeroing in on the next target)

1446
01:05:13,076 --> 01:05:14,743
Bo Been!

1447
01:05:20,483 --> 01:05:21,316
Got it.

1448
01:05:21,317 --> 01:05:22,850
(Targeting Zone 4)

1449
01:05:22,851 --> 01:05:25,020
(Seung Ju)

1450
01:05:25,488 --> 01:05:26,388
Su Yeon, move your feet.

1451
01:05:26,690 --> 01:05:28,423
- Keep moving your feet.
- Serve!

1452
01:05:33,129 --> 01:05:33,962
Mine!

1453
01:05:33,963 --> 01:05:35,130
Sorry!

1454
01:05:35,131 --> 01:05:36,298
A shaky reception!

1455
01:05:37,667 --> 01:05:38,533
That's it!

1456
01:05:39,469 --> 01:05:40,302
Take your time.

1457
01:05:40,603 --> 01:05:41,369
Hit it!

1458
01:05:42,172 --> 01:05:43,305
Into the net!

1459
01:05:43,306 --> 01:05:45,007
(It doesn't clear the net.)

1460
01:05:45,008 --> 01:05:46,309
- She hit it!
- Yes!

1461
01:05:46,310 --> 01:05:47,082
Nice job!

1462
01:05:47,083 --> 01:05:48,310
(First set, Pink Spiders 24
: Wonder Dogs 19)

1463
01:05:50,246 --> 01:05:52,180
- Who knows where this will go?
- They're doing well.

1464
01:05:52,716 --> 01:05:55,051
Come on, what are you doing?

1465
01:05:58,588 --> 01:06:00,856
The Wonder Dogs keep
getting points here and there.

1466
01:06:00,857 --> 01:06:02,925
(Four points straight)

1467
01:06:06,096 --> 01:06:07,063
Na Yeon, get ready to go in.

1468
01:06:10,433 --> 01:06:12,167
(Stay calm.)

1469
01:06:12,168 --> 01:06:15,637
Our serves hit their targets,

1470
01:06:16,373 --> 01:06:18,674
and we started finding our rhythm.

1471
01:06:19,643 --> 01:06:22,411
I started to think we could win.

1472
01:06:23,313 --> 01:06:26,248
- Pick up the energy!
- Yes!

1473
01:06:26,549 --> 01:06:28,984
- Right away!
- Okay!

1474
01:06:29,119 --> 01:06:30,986
- Let's go!
- Let's get one!

1475
01:06:32,489 --> 01:06:34,322
Get the next one!

1476
01:06:35,625 --> 01:06:37,525
Eun Ji, no short serves.

1477
01:06:38,729 --> 01:06:41,497
It's 24 to 19. The gap is down to 5.

1478
01:06:46,136 --> 01:06:47,770
(Target spotted)

1479
01:06:47,804 --> 01:06:49,204
(Next up is...)

1480
01:06:49,205 --> 01:06:51,206
(Zone 2 again.)

1481
01:06:54,144 --> 01:06:55,978
(The target area for the serve)

1482
01:06:56,079 --> 01:06:57,746
Get ready in Zone One.

1483
01:07:04,854 --> 01:07:05,921
The reception is off.

1484
01:07:06,589 --> 01:07:07,343
Seung Ju!

1485
01:07:07,344 --> 01:07:08,156
(An inevitable second touch)

1486
01:07:08,157 --> 01:07:09,157
Here it comes!

1487
01:07:09,259 --> 01:07:10,826
She tips it, but it gets blocked.

1488
01:07:12,162 --> 01:07:13,129
They just send it back over.

1489
01:07:13,329 --> 01:07:14,062
Free ball!

1490
01:07:14,531 --> 01:07:15,431
Send it back.

1491
01:07:15,432 --> 01:07:17,399
- Da Sol pushes it to the left.
- Nice!

1492
01:07:17,801 --> 01:07:19,335
Take it slow.

1493
01:07:20,336 --> 01:07:21,269
Don't rush it.

1494
01:07:24,507 --> 01:07:25,740
They can't get it over!

1495
01:07:28,077 --> 01:07:31,112
(The tough serve forces an error.)

1496
01:07:31,181 --> 01:07:32,581
The score is 20 to 24!

1497
01:07:33,716 --> 01:07:36,851
(Five points straight)

1498
01:07:37,287 --> 01:07:38,387
(Exasperated)

1499
01:07:38,388 --> 01:07:40,456
Take your time! Come on!

1500
01:07:41,591 --> 01:07:44,059
Keep it going!

1501
01:07:44,560 --> 01:07:47,029
Goodness! I'm getting my hopes up.

1502
01:07:47,030 --> 01:07:50,465
That's right.
The first set isn't over yet.

1503
01:07:51,002 --> 01:07:51,967
Wait for it.

1504
01:07:51,968 --> 01:07:54,236
We can catch them. Let's do it!

1505
01:07:55,038 --> 01:07:57,707
Get the ball up high so we can attack!

1506
01:07:57,708 --> 01:07:58,941
(Signaling for a substitution)

1507
01:07:59,309 --> 01:08:00,875
This is driving me crazy.

1508
01:08:00,877 --> 01:08:04,513
Another double substitution.

1509
01:08:04,514 --> 01:08:05,981
(Na Yeon returns to the court.)

1510
01:08:06,983 --> 01:08:09,484
We should get the serve off quickly.

1511
01:08:12,288 --> 01:08:14,589
Keep it going!

1512
01:08:14,792 --> 01:08:16,892
Ho Bin, it's okay. Stay calm!

1513
01:08:17,694 --> 01:08:20,429
It's okay. Just one more point.

1514
01:08:22,198 --> 01:08:24,132
(Moving forward slowly)

1515
01:08:24,501 --> 01:08:27,470
(Hunting for the next target)

1516
01:08:34,110 --> 01:08:35,377
(Target acquired)

1517
01:08:36,412 --> 01:08:37,445
Bo Been.

1518
01:08:38,748 --> 01:08:40,281
- Coach Kim is...
- Yes.

1519
01:08:40,282 --> 01:08:41,417
calling out the serve target.

1520
01:08:41,418 --> 01:08:42,953
Bo Been, be in position early.

1521
01:08:42,954 --> 01:08:44,753
Watch out for a set feint!

1522
01:08:45,989 --> 01:08:47,523
Bo Been's fifth serve.

1523
01:08:47,524 --> 01:08:48,724
(Bo Been's fifth straight serve)

1524
01:08:51,394 --> 01:08:52,828
(Did it catch the net?)

1525
01:08:53,596 --> 01:08:56,965
(No!)

1526
01:09:02,605 --> 01:09:05,207
(Service ace by Bo Been)

1527
01:09:05,775 --> 01:09:08,276
Just a few more!

1528
01:09:10,580 --> 01:09:13,515
It drops!

1529
01:09:13,516 --> 01:09:14,783
What a serve from Bo Been!

1530
01:09:15,518 --> 01:09:16,651
(So proud)

1531
01:09:17,921 --> 01:09:20,155
I thought it caught the net.

1532
01:09:20,523 --> 01:09:23,692
(Six points straight)

1533
01:09:23,693 --> 01:09:25,259
(The Wonder Dogs are gaining ground.)

1534
01:09:25,260 --> 01:09:28,029
- The momentum has really shifted.
- It sure has.

1535
01:09:28,030 --> 01:09:30,132
(The gap is down to three points.)

1536
01:09:30,133 --> 01:09:31,766
- Nice job!
- You're doing great!

1537
01:09:32,035 --> 01:09:35,137
We can catch up to them! We have to!

1538
01:09:36,706 --> 01:09:38,240
Hye Rim, if you make careless mistakes
like that,

1539
01:09:38,241 --> 01:09:39,308
how can I count on you next time?

1540
01:09:39,309 --> 01:09:40,042
Got it.

1541
01:09:40,343 --> 01:09:42,077
We still have a timeout left, right?

1542
01:09:42,845 --> 01:09:44,012
- Want me to call it?
- Not yet.

1543
01:09:44,714 --> 01:09:47,983
For the Pink Spiders,
it may be just one point,

1544
01:09:48,151 --> 01:09:50,885
but the pressure to win that point
just keeps building.

1545
01:09:50,886 --> 01:09:54,356
Don't worry. We're fine!

1546
01:09:59,529 --> 01:10:02,397
Ready! Stay focused to the end!

1547
01:10:04,234 --> 01:10:06,035
The score is 21 to 24.

1548
01:10:24,020 --> 01:10:25,988
(Targeting Zone 3 again)

1549
01:10:26,489 --> 01:10:28,857
(The target area for the serve)

1550
01:10:29,759 --> 01:10:31,927
(Bo Been's sixth serve)

1551
01:10:32,795 --> 01:10:35,096
(Steadying her breath)

1552
01:10:43,506 --> 01:10:44,406
Out!

1553
01:10:46,909 --> 01:10:50,011
A service error ends the first set.

1554
01:10:50,012 --> 01:10:51,145
That went too long.

1555
01:10:52,482 --> 01:10:54,116
I'm sorry.

1556
01:10:54,117 --> 01:10:55,384
Let's focus on the serves.

1557
01:10:56,419 --> 01:10:57,586
- Come here, everyone.
- That was close.

1558
01:10:58,387 --> 01:11:00,054
This is driving me crazy.

1559
01:11:00,590 --> 01:11:04,126
The Pink Spiders take the first set.

1560
01:11:04,360 --> 01:11:05,860
(Strategy session for the second set)

1561
01:11:05,861 --> 01:11:06,829
Sorry.

1562
01:11:06,830 --> 01:11:08,496
Come over here.

1563
01:11:08,497 --> 01:11:09,931
- Everybody, come here!
- Gather around.

1564
01:11:15,304 --> 01:11:18,473
What made those last 4 to 5 points go
so well?

1565
01:11:18,708 --> 01:11:20,376
- Our serves.
- We picked our serve targets,

1566
01:11:20,377 --> 01:11:22,144
- and that got us those points.
- Yes.

1567
01:11:22,145 --> 01:11:24,012
If our serves don't work, we can't win.

1568
01:11:24,013 --> 01:11:26,281
- Yes, Coach!
- We have to hit our targets.

1569
01:11:26,282 --> 01:11:27,082
- Yes!
- Yes!

1570
01:11:27,083 --> 01:11:29,117
Are they doing anything
we didn't talk about?

1571
01:11:29,118 --> 01:11:30,118
- No.
- Exactly.

1572
01:11:30,119 --> 01:11:31,920
They're playing just as we expected.

1573
01:11:32,290 --> 01:11:33,755
We have to stay with them early.

1574
01:11:33,890 --> 01:11:35,558
If we fall behind early, we're in trouble.

1575
01:11:35,559 --> 01:11:37,159
We can do this if we limit our errors.

1576
01:11:37,160 --> 01:11:38,694
- Got it!
- One point at a time.

1577
01:11:38,962 --> 01:11:40,095
Let's play with no regrets!

1578
01:11:41,130 --> 01:11:42,130
Come here, everyone.

1579
01:11:42,131 --> 01:11:43,131
(Meanwhile, the Pink Spiders' huddle)

1580
01:11:43,400 --> 01:11:46,568
When we have a good rhythm,

1581
01:11:46,769 --> 01:11:49,471
if we lose focus, we give them an opening.

1582
01:11:49,472 --> 01:11:51,840
Stay locked in and do what you need to do.

1583
01:11:51,841 --> 01:11:53,875
Stick to the plan, and we'll be fine.

1584
01:11:53,876 --> 01:11:54,676
Got it?

1585
01:11:55,044 --> 01:11:57,746
Forget everything about the last set,

1586
01:11:57,747 --> 01:12:00,181
and let's start fresh.

1587
01:12:00,182 --> 01:12:01,784
Don't think about what happened before.

1588
01:12:01,785 --> 01:12:03,451
Let's stick to the basics.

1589
01:12:03,452 --> 01:12:04,886
Just like we did early on,

1590
01:12:04,887 --> 01:12:07,455
keep communicating and stay focused.

1591
01:12:07,456 --> 01:12:09,758
And Hye Rim, no more mistakes like that.
Stay sharp.

1592
01:12:09,759 --> 01:12:11,526
- Okay!
- We need to come out strong!

1593
01:12:11,527 --> 01:12:13,061
- Let's go!
- Let's have fun out there.

1594
01:12:13,262 --> 01:12:14,095
In 1, 2, 3!

1595
01:12:14,096 --> 01:12:14,963
- Let's do this!
- Let's go!

1596
01:12:14,964 --> 01:12:17,632
- Let's go!
- Let's go! Fresh start!

1597
01:12:17,633 --> 01:12:20,101
The Wonder Dogs get ready
for the second set.

1598
01:12:20,269 --> 01:12:23,137
For middle blocker, Ho Bin is coming out,

1599
01:12:23,138 --> 01:12:25,240
and Ye Dam is going in.

1600
01:12:25,241 --> 01:12:26,741
At 185 cm,

1601
01:12:26,742 --> 01:12:29,277
she's the tallest player
on the Wonder Dogs.

1602
01:12:30,513 --> 01:12:34,516
Ye Dam brings height...

1603
01:12:34,517 --> 01:12:38,920
and plenty of attacking potential,

1604
01:12:39,256 --> 01:12:41,457
which was exactly what we needed.

1605
01:12:41,458 --> 01:12:43,124
We needed to change things up.

1606
01:12:43,292 --> 01:12:44,960
Let's go!

1607
01:12:44,961 --> 01:12:47,362
Chae Rim, right away! Come on!

1608
01:12:48,130 --> 01:12:50,932
(They must beat their former teammates.)

1609
01:12:50,933 --> 01:12:51,933
I'll take the short ones.

1610
01:12:52,568 --> 01:12:54,068
- Get in position!
- Yes.

1611
01:12:55,004 --> 01:12:57,739
(Second set, Pink Spiders 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

1612
01:12:58,941 --> 01:13:01,175
Na Yeon serves to open the second set.

1613
01:13:02,144 --> 01:13:03,277
Hyo Rim,

1614
01:13:03,412 --> 01:13:04,712
you can set it to Ye Dam.

1615
01:13:05,982 --> 01:13:08,483
Ye Dam, use your height to hammer it down!

1616
01:13:08,484 --> 01:13:09,217
Got it!

1617
01:13:12,321 --> 01:13:13,288
The second set begins.

1618
01:13:13,756 --> 01:13:15,323
- Mine!
- Chae Rim receives!

1619
01:13:15,324 --> 01:13:16,491
Ye Dam, go!

1620
01:13:16,492 --> 01:13:18,126
- Go!
- Hyo Rim.

1621
01:13:21,197 --> 01:13:23,131
A quick attack by Ye Dam!

1622
01:13:23,399 --> 01:13:25,400
- Good job!
- Nice one!

1623
01:13:26,435 --> 01:13:30,138
(That's what I'm talking about!)

1624
01:13:31,307 --> 01:13:33,675
("Damdadi" plays in the background.)

1625
01:13:33,676 --> 01:13:34,709
Go, Ye Dam!

1626
01:13:34,910 --> 01:13:37,144
- Nice one, Ye Dam!
- Great job!

1627
01:13:37,380 --> 01:13:39,649
- Nice!
- Way to go!

1628
01:13:39,650 --> 01:13:42,351
Na Yeon, that's all they've got.

1629
01:13:42,352 --> 01:13:43,452
They just hit straight down.

1630
01:13:46,155 --> 01:13:47,124
(Now it's our turn to serve.)

1631
01:13:47,125 --> 01:13:49,491
They're going after them again.
Enkhsoyol is up to serve.

1632
01:13:50,559 --> 01:13:53,861
- Service ace, Enkhsoyol!
- Service ace, Enkhsoyol!

1633
01:13:53,862 --> 01:13:55,862
Serve between them.

1634
01:13:59,505 --> 01:14:01,605
Keep your eyes on the net cord!

1635
01:14:09,738 --> 01:14:10,905
Seriously...

1636
01:14:13,672 --> 01:14:14,715
This is driving me crazy.

1637
01:14:15,438 --> 01:14:18,938
(We knew it.)

1638
01:14:19,305 --> 01:14:21,272
I'll get the next one.

1639
01:14:23,972 --> 01:14:25,166
Seung Ju is serving.

1640
01:14:26,705 --> 01:14:28,038
Watch out for the hard-driven ball!

1641
01:14:28,805 --> 01:14:31,738
(Feeling nervous)

1642
01:14:36,938 --> 01:14:37,872
Tough reception!

1643
01:14:39,238 --> 01:14:40,272
Young In goes for the tip.

1644
01:14:40,272 --> 01:14:41,372
Defended by Na Yeon's dig!

1645
01:14:41,605 --> 01:14:42,972
Cover!

1646
01:14:43,338 --> 01:14:44,272
(Sliding)

1647
01:14:45,038 --> 01:14:46,038
Drifting right!

1648
01:14:46,038 --> 01:14:47,638
Da Eun fires down the line!

1649
01:14:47,638 --> 01:14:48,572
Great touch on defense!

1650
01:14:49,538 --> 01:14:50,472
Underhand bump set.

1651
01:14:50,472 --> 01:14:52,238
Slow it down. Watch the tip!

1652
01:14:52,672 --> 01:14:53,572
Chae Rim swings!

1653
01:14:54,072 --> 01:14:55,272
Eun Ji digs it out!

1654
01:14:55,938 --> 01:14:57,472
Tip incoming!

1655
01:14:58,572 --> 01:14:59,738
(A tip received successfully)

1656
01:15:00,005 --> 01:15:01,738
- Chae Rim!
- Put it away!

1657
01:15:02,272 --> 01:15:03,296
Swing!

1658
01:15:04,372 --> 01:15:05,238
Back Chae Rim!

1659
01:15:05,238 --> 01:15:06,272
She plays the rebound!

1660
01:15:06,278 --> 01:15:07,711
Hyo Rim with the back set.

1661
01:15:08,320 --> 01:15:09,047
Feeding Young In on the outside!

1662
01:15:09,638 --> 01:15:11,305
Defended, but stuffed at the net!

1663
01:15:11,705 --> 01:15:12,538
Hey!

1664
01:15:14,305 --> 01:15:15,172
Nice!

1665
01:15:16,272 --> 01:15:17,672
Great hustle!

1666
01:15:21,372 --> 01:15:22,405
Hyo Rim,

1667
01:15:22,405 --> 01:15:24,672
deliver a clean ball.

1668
01:15:24,672 --> 01:15:25,705
Stay ready!

1669
01:15:28,305 --> 01:15:30,005
Let's go!

1670
01:15:30,305 --> 01:15:32,172
Right back in!

1671
01:15:34,805 --> 01:15:35,940
Seung Ju back at the service line.

1672
01:15:39,738 --> 01:15:40,538
Ye Dam!

1673
01:15:41,005 --> 01:15:41,905
Late on the approach!

1674
01:15:45,038 --> 01:15:46,853
Solid double block,
and the rebound falls to Eun Ji!

1675
01:15:47,438 --> 01:15:48,448
She swings right in place.

1676
01:15:48,805 --> 01:15:50,005
Hyo Rim digs it out.

1677
01:15:50,005 --> 01:15:51,072
The ball is a bit off the net.

1678
01:15:52,705 --> 01:15:54,072
She pushes it across.

1679
01:15:55,172 --> 01:15:56,658
Su Yeon takes the second touch.

1680
01:15:57,872 --> 01:15:59,872
- Hyo Rim keeps it alive again!
- That's it!

1681
01:16:00,305 --> 01:16:01,705
(Young In gets ready to attack.)

1682
01:16:01,705 --> 01:16:02,805
Seon Ah handles the free ball.

1683
01:16:02,805 --> 01:16:03,705
Young In swings!

1684
01:16:06,405 --> 01:16:07,538
Dug again!

1685
01:16:07,538 --> 01:16:08,505
Put it down!

1686
01:16:09,238 --> 01:16:10,038
Lee Na Yeon.

1687
01:16:15,238 --> 01:16:16,272
Why tip that?

1688
01:16:16,538 --> 01:16:17,938
What was that look?

1689
01:16:18,372 --> 01:16:19,788
What do you think you're on the court for?

1690
01:16:22,372 --> 01:16:23,172
Understood.

1691
01:16:23,172 --> 01:16:26,638
(Attacks are not working out.)

1692
01:16:27,272 --> 01:16:29,205
(Rally continues.)

1693
01:16:31,037 --> 01:16:31,871
Back set!

1694
01:16:31,872 --> 01:16:32,838
It's way too low.

1695
01:16:34,572 --> 01:16:35,905
Another off-the-block rebound!

1696
01:16:36,472 --> 01:16:37,338
Free ball over!

1697
01:16:38,072 --> 01:16:39,205
(A squandered chance for attack)

1698
01:16:39,205 --> 01:16:40,372
Dug up!

1699
01:16:40,905 --> 01:16:41,672
Choi Eun Ji.

1700
01:16:43,338 --> 01:16:44,905
They managed to save this ball.

1701
01:16:44,906 --> 01:16:45,778
Spike.

1702
01:16:45,779 --> 01:16:46,612
(Blocked)

1703
01:16:47,238 --> 01:16:48,544
Ball pushed out to the left pin!

1704
01:16:49,205 --> 01:16:50,038
(Blocked again)

1705
01:16:50,038 --> 01:16:50,938
Kept off the floor!

1706
01:16:51,405 --> 01:16:52,305
It goes to the left again.

1707
01:16:54,472 --> 01:16:55,438
Swing through!

1708
01:16:56,305 --> 01:16:57,505
Spike!

1709
01:16:57,505 --> 01:16:58,405
Back Chae Rim.

1710
01:16:58,872 --> 01:16:59,772
There we go!

1711
01:17:00,405 --> 01:17:02,138
Why are we so late on our timing?

1712
01:17:02,138 --> 01:17:03,505
Pick up your feet!

1713
01:17:04,305 --> 01:17:06,338
Wonder Dogs finally put one away!

1714
01:17:06,338 --> 01:17:08,805
(Second set, Pink Spiders 4:
Wonder Dogs 2)

1715
01:17:13,538 --> 01:17:15,172
(Eyeing)

1716
01:17:16,272 --> 01:17:17,205
Watch those middle attacks!

1717
01:17:20,472 --> 01:17:22,372
(Ye Dam serves.)

1718
01:17:22,838 --> 01:17:23,805
Clean pass.

1719
01:17:24,805 --> 01:17:26,066
Na Yeon dishes the back set.

1720
01:17:29,305 --> 01:17:30,238
It hits right in the middle.

1721
01:17:31,305 --> 01:17:34,005
Sweet connection, Na Yeon!

1722
01:17:35,872 --> 01:17:37,205
(Glancing)

1723
01:17:37,206 --> 01:17:39,639
Why are you staying on the floor?
Jump and contest!

1724
01:17:40,572 --> 01:17:42,338
Na Yeon pushes it out to the left pin.

1725
01:17:43,305 --> 01:17:44,205
It's a touch out.

1726
01:17:44,905 --> 01:17:47,138
Pink Spiders keep it off the hardwood!

1727
01:17:47,138 --> 01:17:48,505
Sneaky tip!

1728
01:17:48,972 --> 01:17:50,405
(Giving up another point to a block)

1729
01:17:50,838 --> 01:17:52,005
How did that happen?

1730
01:17:52,005 --> 01:17:53,472
(Second set, Pink Spiders 8:
Wonder Dogs 5)

1731
01:17:53,472 --> 01:17:57,405
Throughout the second set,
nothing seemed to click.

1732
01:17:57,672 --> 01:18:01,305
Our receiving, digging, setting, and
hitting are all completely breaking down.

1733
01:18:01,672 --> 01:18:03,838
I just kept racking my brain
on how to solve it.

1734
01:18:03,838 --> 01:18:05,305
(We must turn this around.)

1735
01:18:06,638 --> 01:18:08,538
I'm pinning myself against the antenna.

1736
01:18:10,372 --> 01:18:13,305
(Eagle eye activated)

1737
01:18:14,472 --> 01:18:15,738
Enkhsoyol!

1738
01:18:17,605 --> 01:18:19,872
Take it down the line!

1739
01:18:21,438 --> 01:18:24,605
(The target is the short blocker.)

1740
01:18:26,505 --> 01:18:28,972
(Here it comes.)

1741
01:18:29,405 --> 01:18:31,072
It's Eun Ji's turn to serve.

1742
01:18:34,372 --> 01:18:35,372
Run the C-quick!

1743
01:18:38,272 --> 01:18:39,572
(Enkhsoyol versus...)

1744
01:18:39,572 --> 01:18:41,372
(Na Yeon)

1745
01:18:42,279 --> 01:18:43,945
- Hit it!
- Hit it from the left pin!

1746
01:18:43,946 --> 01:18:45,437
(Enkhsoyol wins!)

1747
01:18:45,438 --> 01:18:46,838
Great touch! Keep this momentum!

1748
01:18:48,838 --> 01:18:51,272
(Second set, Pink Spiders 10:
Wonder Dogs 6)

1749
01:18:52,205 --> 01:18:53,038
Enkhsoyol!

1750
01:18:53,605 --> 01:18:54,738
(One more time!)

1751
01:18:54,738 --> 01:18:55,672
Got it.

1752
01:18:56,372 --> 01:18:57,372
Let's run it over here.

1753
01:18:57,372 --> 01:19:00,705
(Na Yeon still guards the front.)

1754
01:19:03,705 --> 01:19:05,138
(Good reception)

1755
01:19:05,138 --> 01:19:06,005
Put it away!

1756
01:19:06,005 --> 01:19:07,405
(The second round...)

1757
01:19:07,405 --> 01:19:08,872
(begins.)

1758
01:19:10,305 --> 01:19:11,272
Spike!

1759
01:19:15,805 --> 01:19:17,972
Wonder Dogs on the board!

1760
01:19:18,705 --> 01:19:20,538
Not another point!

1761
01:19:22,372 --> 01:19:24,372
Let's go!

1762
01:19:25,105 --> 01:19:27,238
Momentum is swinging their way!

1763
01:19:29,072 --> 01:19:30,872
(Wonder Dogs side)

1764
01:19:30,872 --> 01:19:32,872
(Pink Spiders side)

1765
01:19:33,705 --> 01:19:36,538
(Eagle still hungers.)

1766
01:19:37,638 --> 01:19:39,572
(Directing the serve target)

1767
01:19:43,538 --> 01:19:44,938
(Ha Hyo Rim serves.)

1768
01:19:46,772 --> 01:19:48,972
(Ball high up in the air!)

1769
01:19:53,305 --> 01:19:54,672
(Straight to a push shot)

1770
01:19:55,038 --> 01:19:57,572
Pushed deep into the side!

1771
01:20:00,405 --> 01:20:04,438
(The momentum has shifted.)

1772
01:20:04,972 --> 01:20:08,538
(Second set, Pink Spiders 11
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1773
01:20:13,038 --> 01:20:15,038
(This momentum must go on.)

1774
01:20:16,304 --> 01:20:19,072
(Time for a sub)

1775
01:20:22,705 --> 01:20:25,972
Coach Kim subs out the opposite hitter.

1776
01:20:34,238 --> 01:20:35,105
I need to make a change.

1777
01:20:35,538 --> 01:20:36,305
Get Da Sol up.

1778
01:20:36,638 --> 01:20:38,372
(Another sub?)

1779
01:20:38,372 --> 01:20:40,272
Call Da Sol over!

1780
01:20:41,672 --> 01:20:43,405
(In a rush)

1781
01:20:44,172 --> 01:20:47,505
(Experienced coach pulls up another card.)

1782
01:20:48,072 --> 01:20:51,672
A setter's role sets the tone
for the entire match.

1783
01:20:52,105 --> 01:20:57,038
Da Sol has plenty of big-game experience.

1784
01:20:57,705 --> 01:21:01,705
I hoped she could bring
calm and stability to our rhythm.

1785
01:21:02,438 --> 01:21:05,238
This was my very first look on the floor.

1786
01:21:05,238 --> 01:21:08,438
So I wanted to show everything I had.

1787
01:21:08,438 --> 01:21:12,372
More than anything,
I was desperate to beat the Pink Spiders.

1788
01:21:13,472 --> 01:21:14,572
No need to get jittery.

1789
01:21:14,572 --> 01:21:16,572
They don't have anything we don't have.

1790
01:21:16,572 --> 01:21:17,405
Got it?

1791
01:21:17,405 --> 01:21:19,472
(While Da Sol prepares for a sub)

1792
01:21:21,238 --> 01:21:23,305
(The score gap widens again.)

1793
01:21:24,138 --> 01:21:26,105
(Second set, Pink Spiders 12
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1794
01:21:26,772 --> 01:21:28,672
Enkhsoyol gets roofed!

1795
01:21:29,672 --> 01:21:31,605
(Second set, Pink Spiders 13
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1796
01:21:34,372 --> 01:21:35,805
(Substitute them.)

1797
01:21:36,105 --> 01:21:37,038
Go get them, Da Sol!

1798
01:21:37,038 --> 01:21:38,172
Show them what you've got!

1799
01:21:39,605 --> 01:21:40,638
Hyo Rim checks out,

1800
01:21:40,638 --> 01:21:42,105
and Da Sol checks in.

1801
01:21:42,805 --> 01:21:44,972
Chae Rim!

1802
01:21:44,972 --> 01:21:46,205
Da Sol faces her old Pink Spiders squad...

1803
01:21:46,205 --> 01:21:48,938
after stepping away from the pros.

1804
01:21:49,305 --> 01:21:52,605
Right as Na Yeon signed
with the Pink Spiders,

1805
01:21:52,605 --> 01:21:56,072
Da Sol parted ways with that very club.

1806
01:21:57,004 --> 01:21:58,904
Last year, I was on that side of the net.

1807
01:21:58,904 --> 01:22:00,204
Now, I'm standing right here.

1808
01:22:01,037 --> 01:22:06,004
I really wanted to prove
what I can still do out there.

1809
01:22:06,537 --> 01:22:08,670
(Na Yeon serves.)

1810
01:22:09,604 --> 01:22:12,204
Just focus on keeping that pass up.

1811
01:22:12,204 --> 01:22:13,070
If it gets out of system,

1812
01:22:13,070 --> 01:22:14,804
don't sweat it. I'll clean it up.

1813
01:22:18,904 --> 01:22:20,004
(Good reception)

1814
01:22:20,537 --> 01:22:21,637
Feed Yeon Joo!

1815
01:22:22,937 --> 01:22:24,670
(Da Sol's back toss)

1816
01:22:25,070 --> 01:22:27,270
(The Flame Deer launched)

1817
01:22:29,737 --> 01:22:31,570
(Block touch out)

1818
01:22:31,570 --> 01:22:32,637
Beautiful!

1819
01:22:32,970 --> 01:22:37,804
(A satisfying score
right after substitution)

1820
01:22:38,504 --> 01:22:39,804
Da Sol's release is short and fast.

1821
01:22:39,804 --> 01:22:40,937
I overcommitted on that one.

1822
01:22:41,237 --> 01:22:43,870
We can't let this run get away from us.

1823
01:22:43,870 --> 01:22:47,104
Da Sol just served notice
to her former team...

1824
01:22:47,104 --> 01:22:48,670
of what she brings to the table.

1825
01:22:49,370 --> 01:22:50,937
It's 9 to 13, 4 points behind.

1826
01:22:55,570 --> 01:22:57,204
(Enkhsoyol serves.)

1827
01:22:57,870 --> 01:22:58,670
Heavy serve coming in!

1828
01:22:58,970 --> 01:23:00,370
(The ball makes it to Na Yeon!)

1829
01:23:00,370 --> 01:23:01,337
Na Yeon handles the ball.

1830
01:23:03,637 --> 01:23:04,604
Quick attack!

1831
01:23:05,237 --> 01:23:06,670
(A quick attack to the middle)

1832
01:23:07,070 --> 01:23:09,004
(Ye Dam blocks it.)

1833
01:23:09,104 --> 01:23:10,004
Stuff block!

1834
01:23:10,004 --> 01:23:12,237
Try going through the middle,
and they're getting shut down!

1835
01:23:12,537 --> 01:23:14,270
(Court will be defended at all costs.)

1836
01:23:14,537 --> 01:23:16,570
Lee Ye Dam is an absolute brick wall!

1837
01:23:18,237 --> 01:23:20,070
I was lying in wait for that exact ball.

1838
01:23:20,937 --> 01:23:22,870
Ye Dam just shut down the entire net!

1839
01:23:24,637 --> 01:23:26,937
Na Yeon looks completely caught off guard.

1840
01:23:26,937 --> 01:23:30,270
This is our chance
for Da Sol to step on the gas.

1841
01:23:32,204 --> 01:23:33,104
Na Yeon!

1842
01:23:33,104 --> 01:23:34,537
Dig it out and feed Seung Ju on the pin!

1843
01:23:35,504 --> 01:23:36,637
Only after we control the first contact!

1844
01:23:39,970 --> 01:23:41,837
The score sits at 13 to 10.

1845
01:23:46,084 --> 01:23:46,950
(Shaken up!)

1846
01:23:46,951 --> 01:23:47,652
Nice serve.

1847
01:23:47,770 --> 01:23:48,504
Su Yeon passes the serve.

1848
01:23:48,973 --> 01:23:50,040
(A quick, high set)

1849
01:23:50,211 --> 01:23:51,144
Pyo Seung Ju.

1850
01:23:51,145 --> 01:23:52,445
(Pyo Seung Ju charges forward.)

1851
01:23:54,882 --> 01:23:55,849
She gets it.

1852
01:23:57,418 --> 01:24:01,962
(The defense is broken through.)

1853
01:24:01,999 --> 01:24:03,666
Na Yeon sets the ball to...

1854
01:24:03,667 --> 01:24:05,368
Seung Ju incredibly quickly.

1855
01:24:05,369 --> 01:24:07,236
Our players couldn't react in time.

1856
01:24:07,638 --> 01:24:08,705
One right away.

1857
01:24:11,208 --> 01:24:12,442
Enkhsoyol.

1858
01:24:12,877 --> 01:24:14,578
- Get ready, Enkhsoyol.
- Okay.

1859
01:24:15,413 --> 01:24:16,646
- I'll jump quicker.
- Okay.

1860
01:24:17,481 --> 01:24:20,049
(Pyo Seung Ju serves.)

1861
01:24:21,312 --> 01:24:22,146
(Solid receive)

1862
01:24:22,480 --> 01:24:23,713
(The Flame Deer is ready.)

1863
01:24:23,714 --> 01:24:24,748
(A back-row set)

1864
01:24:24,749 --> 01:24:25,715
Hwang Yeon Joo.

1865
01:24:26,584 --> 01:24:27,918
(The ball shoots high into the air.)

1866
01:24:28,453 --> 01:24:29,319
Oh, my.

1867
01:24:30,589 --> 01:24:32,056
Seung Ju runs and keeps it alive.

1868
01:24:32,057 --> 01:24:33,824
There's no way they can
attack from that position.

1869
01:24:33,825 --> 01:24:34,658
(It's a free ball.)

1870
01:24:34,659 --> 01:24:36,526
- Set it up.
- Another back-row set.

1871
01:24:37,863 --> 01:24:38,596
Set it up.

1872
01:24:38,597 --> 01:24:39,463
(Now, to the left.)

1873
01:24:39,464 --> 01:24:40,799
This time, to the other side.

1874
01:24:41,566 --> 01:24:42,533
I'll take it.

1875
01:24:42,868 --> 01:24:43,734
The ball goes over.

1876
01:24:43,735 --> 01:24:44,401
(It went over.)

1877
01:24:45,003 --> 01:24:45,803
Eun Ji.

1878
01:24:46,638 --> 01:24:47,471
(Effortlessly)

1879
01:24:48,406 --> 01:24:49,206
Enkhsoyol.

1880
01:24:49,908 --> 01:24:51,609
- Get ready, Enkhsoyol.
- Okay.

1881
01:24:51,610 --> 01:24:52,443
Enkhsoyol.

1882
01:24:54,242 --> 01:24:55,812
(Enkhsoyol leaps into the air.)

1883
01:24:56,047 --> 01:24:57,180
Take your time.

1884
01:24:58,383 --> 01:25:00,551
Back-row attack.

1885
01:25:00,786 --> 01:25:02,953
(The timing was off.)

1886
01:25:03,321 --> 01:25:05,856
(Oh my.)

1887
01:25:05,857 --> 01:25:08,992
Da Sol, if you can't set it,
just catch and throw.

1888
01:25:09,861 --> 01:25:11,719
Our bodies aren't moving fast enough.

1889
01:25:11,744 --> 01:25:12,864
(Their attacks keep getting blocked.)

1890
01:25:15,567 --> 01:25:17,467
I felt like I could do more.

1891
01:25:18,169 --> 01:25:21,238
But my body just wouldn't keep up.

1892
01:25:21,873 --> 01:25:23,073
It was frustrating.

1893
01:25:24,509 --> 01:25:25,476
(The match continues.)

1894
01:25:25,477 --> 01:25:26,543
It's a long one.

1895
01:25:27,679 --> 01:25:28,578
Choi Eun Ji.

1896
01:25:28,881 --> 01:25:30,514
She ran over and got it.

1897
01:25:31,683 --> 01:25:32,549
Set it up.

1898
01:25:32,751 --> 01:25:33,584
Hwang Yeon Joo.

1899
01:25:35,353 --> 01:25:36,219
It's out.

1900
01:25:36,220 --> 01:25:37,454
(The ball goes straight out.)

1901
01:25:37,923 --> 01:25:40,358
I'm starting to get the hang of it.

1902
01:25:42,994 --> 01:25:44,761
One right away.

1903
01:25:46,531 --> 01:25:47,631
We're down by seven.

1904
01:25:47,632 --> 01:25:48,499
(Second set, Pink Spiders 17
: Wonder Dogs 10)

1905
01:25:52,070 --> 01:25:53,103
Please, just one.

1906
01:25:56,775 --> 01:25:58,908
Please, let's get one point at a time.

1907
01:26:00,278 --> 01:26:01,545
She attacks from the back.

1908
01:26:01,546 --> 01:26:02,546
Get it.

1909
01:26:03,248 --> 01:26:05,183
I haven't had a chance
to show what I can do yet.

1910
01:26:08,219 --> 01:26:09,119
Come on.

1911
01:26:16,227 --> 01:26:17,060
Get it.

1912
01:26:17,061 --> 01:26:19,629
(The ball finally lands inside the court.)

1913
01:26:19,998 --> 01:26:22,399
(Second set, Pink Spiders 19
: Wonder Dogs 11)

1914
01:26:22,701 --> 01:26:24,101
One more right away.

1915
01:26:24,703 --> 01:26:25,603
My bad.

1916
01:26:26,838 --> 01:26:27,938
Let's go.

1917
01:26:27,939 --> 01:26:30,307
(She wants to show them
what she's capable of,)

1918
01:26:30,976 --> 01:26:35,079
(but the score keeps slipping
further away.)

1919
01:26:41,519 --> 01:26:42,520
Hyo Rim.

1920
01:26:45,290 --> 01:26:50,060
(The setter is finally substituted.)

1921
01:26:50,061 --> 01:26:52,463
- Where were you?
- At the back.

1922
01:26:53,232 --> 01:26:55,065
Setter Hyo Rim is back on the court.

1923
01:26:55,066 --> 01:26:56,533
(Kim Da Sol out, Ha Hyo Rim in)

1924
01:26:56,968 --> 01:27:00,470
She gave it everything she had,

1925
01:27:00,471 --> 01:27:02,439
when we were in a difficult situation.

1926
01:27:03,008 --> 01:27:04,241
When I stepped onto the court,

1927
01:27:04,476 --> 01:27:07,311
all I could think about was winning.

1928
01:27:11,483 --> 01:27:12,683
Ye Eun receives.

1929
01:27:12,684 --> 01:27:13,748
To the left.

1930
01:27:13,749 --> 01:27:15,419
(Chae Rim's powerful hit)

1931
01:27:16,121 --> 01:27:18,055
Setting it up for Eun Ji. Da Eun gets it.

1932
01:27:19,958 --> 01:27:20,737
It's dug up.

1933
01:27:20,738 --> 01:27:21,725
(Hyo Rim's incredible save)

1934
01:27:22,293 --> 01:27:24,495
(There's no setter available?)

1935
01:27:24,496 --> 01:27:25,395
Mine.

1936
01:27:26,064 --> 01:27:26,897
Hey.

1937
01:27:26,999 --> 01:27:28,231
Chae Seon Ah.

1938
01:27:28,232 --> 01:27:29,299
(Seon Ah makes a second-touch set.)

1939
01:27:29,667 --> 01:27:30,567
Hit it.

1940
01:27:31,261 --> 01:27:32,444
Yeon Joo sends it over.

1941
01:27:32,445 --> 01:27:33,711
- Right.
- She made it.

1942
01:27:33,771 --> 01:27:36,139
(A touch out off the blocker)

1943
01:27:36,975 --> 01:27:38,509
(A quick glance)

1944
01:27:38,829 --> 01:27:42,632
(Their chance to serve again)

1945
01:27:43,214 --> 01:27:45,649
(The eagle takes flight once more.)

1946
01:27:49,387 --> 01:27:51,622
(Instructions to serve
from position three)

1947
01:27:51,956 --> 01:27:54,124
(Okay.)

1948
01:27:55,727 --> 01:27:57,327
(Targeting Seung Ju)

1949
01:27:57,862 --> 01:27:58,795
Yeon Joo delivers a serve.

1950
01:28:03,735 --> 01:28:06,603
(Right on target)

1951
01:28:06,604 --> 01:28:07,771
Hwang Yeon Joo!

1952
01:28:07,772 --> 01:28:12,209
(The Flame Deer serves an ace!)

1953
01:28:15,947 --> 01:28:19,116
Hwang Yeon Joo, she holds the all-time
record for career service aces.

1954
01:28:19,284 --> 01:28:21,418
I've got it.

1955
01:28:21,886 --> 01:28:22,853
That serve dropped short.

1956
01:28:25,223 --> 01:28:26,723
(No mercy)

1957
01:28:26,958 --> 01:28:29,593
(Hunting for the next target)

1958
01:28:34,680 --> 01:28:35,989
(Got it.)

1959
01:28:36,835 --> 01:28:38,135
The score is 13 to 19.

1960
01:28:41,573 --> 01:28:42,339
(Pinpoint serve)

1961
01:28:42,340 --> 01:28:43,374
Shaky reception.

1962
01:28:44,175 --> 01:28:45,046
Eun Ji swings.

1963
01:28:46,044 --> 01:28:47,411
Yeon Joo digs it out!

1964
01:28:47,979 --> 01:28:48,979
Put it away!

1965
01:28:49,180 --> 01:28:50,013
Back Chae Rim!

1966
01:28:50,448 --> 01:28:51,848
Su Yeon dives for the dig!

1967
01:28:52,884 --> 01:28:54,484
Sneaky tip!

1968
01:28:55,053 --> 01:28:55,919
Eun Ji again!

1969
01:28:55,920 --> 01:28:58,789
Ye Eun keeps it alive with a rolling dig!

1970
01:28:59,157 --> 01:29:00,457
Free ball for the Pink Spiders!

1971
01:29:01,793 --> 01:29:02,493
(They cover it again.)

1972
01:29:02,494 --> 01:29:03,494
They just keep keeping it off the floor!

1973
01:29:04,629 --> 01:29:05,629
Stuff block!

1974
01:29:06,965 --> 01:29:07,965
Quick hit from the middle!

1975
01:29:09,100 --> 01:29:10,033
Good!

1976
01:29:11,202 --> 01:29:12,302
Is that coming over?

1977
01:29:12,303 --> 01:29:14,838
(Is it crossing over?)

1978
01:29:15,574 --> 01:29:17,675
Overpass kill!

1979
01:29:18,076 --> 01:29:19,043
(Heartbreaker)

1980
01:29:22,647 --> 01:29:25,916
(Momentum swings right back
to the Pink Spiders.)

1981
01:29:26,684 --> 01:29:27,851
Choi Eun Ji with the finish.

1982
01:29:28,119 --> 01:29:29,252
Hey!

1983
01:29:29,454 --> 01:29:30,787
(Ji Su takes flight.)

1984
01:29:30,856 --> 01:29:31,722
Slide attack!

1985
01:29:32,423 --> 01:29:33,523
Tool off the block!

1986
01:29:33,524 --> 01:29:35,291
(Broken defense)

1987
01:29:35,292 --> 01:29:37,127
Whenever they get out of system like that,

1988
01:29:37,128 --> 01:29:39,662
Na Yeon loves running that slide.

1989
01:29:39,663 --> 01:29:40,764
(Second set, Pink Spiders 21:
Wonder Dogs 13)

1990
01:29:40,765 --> 01:29:41,865
That's heading deep.

1991
01:29:41,866 --> 01:29:43,132
Kept in play!

1992
01:29:43,133 --> 01:29:44,834
(Ball clears the net)

1993
01:29:45,737 --> 01:29:46,603
Dump!

1994
01:29:47,205 --> 01:29:49,673
Hey, Yu Kyung.

1995
01:29:49,908 --> 01:29:52,075
Na Yeon is totally in her groove now.

1996
01:29:52,076 --> 01:29:53,377
(She even succeeds in dumps with ease.)

1997
01:29:53,945 --> 01:29:55,479
Score moves to 22 to 14.

1998
01:29:55,480 --> 01:29:56,880
(Second set, Pink Spiders 22 :
Wonder Dogs 14)

1999
01:29:57,415 --> 01:29:58,415
Eun Ji serving.

2000
01:29:59,517 --> 01:30:00,484
Ace!

2001
01:30:00,485 --> 01:30:02,252
(Eun Ji delivers an ace.)

2002
01:30:02,253 --> 01:30:03,620
Why are we watching that hit the floor?

2003
01:30:03,955 --> 01:30:06,589
That's a routine ball.
Why isn't anyone calling for it?

2004
01:30:07,292 --> 01:30:09,760
- My bad.
- Set point for the Pink Spiders!

2005
01:30:10,628 --> 01:30:12,530
(Pink Spiders at set point)

2006
01:30:12,531 --> 01:30:13,463
Park Min Ji!

2007
01:30:13,464 --> 01:30:15,031
(Na Yeon is on a roll.)

2008
01:30:17,302 --> 01:30:18,869
Quick attack!

2009
01:30:18,870 --> 01:30:21,505
(No answer for Na Yeon's middle attack)

2010
01:30:21,540 --> 01:30:23,941
And that wraps up the second set.

2011
01:30:23,942 --> 01:30:26,910
(Second set, Pink Spiders 25 :
Wonder Dogs 16)

2012
01:30:28,179 --> 01:30:30,213
The second set score is 25 to 16.

2013
01:30:30,214 --> 01:30:31,848
We're down 0 to 2.

2014
01:30:31,849 --> 01:30:33,016
Lock in.

2015
01:30:33,017 --> 01:30:34,518
- Yes!
- Keep your heads in the game.

2016
01:30:34,519 --> 01:30:36,253
- Got it!
- We have to make a push right here.

2017
01:30:36,254 --> 01:30:38,021
Clean slate from this point on.

2018
01:30:40,191 --> 01:30:42,826
I felt a bit rattled.

2019
01:30:43,061 --> 01:30:44,495
Let's reset.

2020
01:30:54,572 --> 01:30:56,473
I honestly don't know
what to say to you right now.

2021
01:30:56,474 --> 01:30:58,271
We aren't doing a single thing
we're capable of.

2022
01:31:06,017 --> 01:31:10,420
(Stunned silence
between coach and players)

2023
01:31:11,689 --> 01:31:13,923
We need to execute
at least one basic thing.

2024
01:31:13,924 --> 01:31:16,226
Serves, blocks, back-row defense...
Nothing is clicking.

2025
01:31:16,427 --> 01:31:18,027
Our setting and offense
are out of sync too.

2026
01:31:18,028 --> 01:31:20,563
What are we supposed to fall back on?

2027
01:31:22,600 --> 01:31:24,100
What do I even do with this?

2028
01:31:24,202 --> 01:31:25,869
I genuinely didn't have an answer.

2029
01:31:27,540 --> 01:31:30,874
Still, they desperately
needed a shock to the system.

2030
01:31:31,242 --> 01:31:33,643
I had to light a fire under them
to turn the tide.

2031
01:31:34,346 --> 01:31:35,412
It's no wonder if we lose this match.

2032
01:31:35,513 --> 01:31:37,380
And if we go down like this today,

2033
01:31:38,816 --> 01:31:41,217
we're heading straight
into post-match conditioning drills.

2034
01:31:43,154 --> 01:31:44,521
(Gulp)

2035
01:31:45,823 --> 01:31:47,725
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2036
01:31:47,726 --> 01:31:48,925
Right back on the court!

2037
01:31:49,094 --> 01:31:50,894
Let's reset!

2038
01:31:51,029 --> 01:31:53,231
I can't speak for anyone else,

2039
01:31:53,232 --> 01:31:54,532
but that snapped me wide awake.

2040
01:31:54,800 --> 01:31:57,067
I want to take this so badly. Let's do it!

2041
01:31:57,068 --> 01:31:59,770
My head was spinning,
but I had to snap out of it.

2042
01:32:00,204 --> 01:32:02,105
If we win this,
we skip extra conditioning.

2043
01:32:02,274 --> 01:32:03,641
Win at all costs!

2044
01:32:03,808 --> 01:32:05,742
Today took everything out of me.

2045
01:32:05,743 --> 01:32:07,511
Who on earth wants to run
extra suicides after a match?

2046
01:32:07,512 --> 01:32:10,213
I thought my brain was about to fry.

2047
01:32:11,049 --> 01:32:12,883
We've totally got this, right?

2048
01:32:12,884 --> 01:32:14,985
Fast feet, cool heads!

2049
01:32:14,986 --> 01:32:15,719
(Steeling their resolve)

2050
01:32:20,592 --> 01:32:23,560
I hate relying on threats
to get players moving.

2051
01:32:23,729 --> 01:32:25,629
It feels cheap and old-school.

2052
01:32:29,267 --> 01:32:31,602
(Weathering the storm)

2053
01:32:31,603 --> 01:32:34,638
I really despise coaching that way.

2054
01:32:35,573 --> 01:32:38,509
It was a desperate outburst as a coach.

2055
01:32:39,444 --> 01:32:43,747
(Following her emotional speech
during the Shujitsu match,)

2056
01:32:44,115 --> 01:32:46,684
(another uncharacteristic
flash of frustration)

2057
01:32:46,685 --> 01:32:47,651
Are you kidding me?

2058
01:32:49,921 --> 01:32:51,888
I keep my resignation letter
in my back pocket.

2059
01:32:53,424 --> 01:32:55,959
(Swapping the resignation letter
for her clipboard)

2060
01:32:56,527 --> 01:32:58,295
(She still has plenty
of adjustments to make.)

2061
01:32:58,596 --> 01:32:59,429
Tae Young.

2062
01:32:59,897 --> 01:33:01,698
Should we just hunt Eun Ji on every serve?

2063
01:33:04,936 --> 01:33:08,939
(She found a solution on the stat sheet.)

2064
01:33:09,540 --> 01:33:11,307
(I got it.)

2065
01:33:11,909 --> 01:33:13,209
(She pops up from the bench)

2066
01:33:13,644 --> 01:33:15,412
Serve Eun Ji exclusively.

2067
01:33:15,413 --> 01:33:17,146
Find her on the court
and target her chest.

2068
01:33:17,147 --> 01:33:18,047
- Understood.
- Got it.

2069
01:33:18,282 --> 01:33:19,148
Enkhsoyol.

2070
01:33:19,317 --> 01:33:21,184
Where did I tell you to place that swing?

2071
01:33:22,153 --> 01:33:23,786
(Pulling Enkhsoyol
aside for a quick review)

2072
01:33:23,787 --> 01:33:25,455
Stop burying it in the net.

2073
01:33:25,856 --> 01:33:30,026
We all know what she's capable of
when she swings with authority.

2074
01:33:30,027 --> 01:33:33,361
This entire offense runs through you.

2075
01:33:34,566 --> 01:33:37,934
Clear your head.

2076
01:33:37,935 --> 01:33:40,036
(Muttering under her breath)

2077
01:33:40,037 --> 01:33:40,937
Got it?

2078
01:33:41,572 --> 01:33:43,473
(Revisiting the film breakdown)

2079
01:33:44,354 --> 01:33:47,183
(Refocusing on driving
sharp cross-court and line shots)

2080
01:33:47,257 --> 01:33:49,373
- Got it?
- I think so.

2081
01:33:49,682 --> 01:33:51,849
- Let's go!
- Make sure of it.

2082
01:33:52,422 --> 01:33:53,789
(Checking Enkhsoyol)

2083
01:33:54,256 --> 01:33:56,856
With Seung Ju and Na Yeon gone,

2084
01:33:56,856 --> 01:33:58,622
I felt like I had to shoulder the load...

2085
01:33:58,622 --> 01:34:00,722
for everything to work out.

2086
01:34:00,722 --> 01:34:06,956
I need to step up and play aggressively
to rack up points.

2087
01:34:07,622 --> 01:34:09,689
Our serves are everything.

2088
01:34:10,222 --> 01:34:12,856
(Keeping an eye on Ye Dam
rather than Enkhsoyol)

2089
01:34:15,322 --> 01:34:19,789
Coach Kim made it clear
that if this set looks like the first two,

2090
01:34:20,089 --> 01:34:23,722
we're going straight
into night conditioning after the match.

2091
01:34:23,722 --> 01:34:25,622
Times like this, we need
to lean on good memories.

2092
01:34:25,622 --> 01:34:27,789
Remember the Shujitsu match.

2093
01:34:27,789 --> 01:34:29,722
Exactly. A comeback is still on the table.

2094
01:34:30,789 --> 01:34:33,256
(Either we find a way
to turn this around...)

2095
01:34:34,522 --> 01:34:37,522
(or we get crushed by our former members.)

2096
01:34:37,956 --> 01:34:40,156
(Hyo Rim serves.)

2097
01:34:40,156 --> 01:34:43,022
Put every serve on Eun Ji.

2098
01:34:43,022 --> 01:34:46,556
(Serve target: Choi Eun Ji)

2099
